ct_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S1.F1.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\displaystyle\mathbf{e}_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle\mathbf{e}_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="fill:none" d="M 356.84 -77.83"></path><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 358.4 -85.54)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.98em;--ltx-fo-height:0.44em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" height="8.23" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 6.15)" width="13.5"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S1.F1.pic1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\displaystyle\mathbf{e}_{4}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle\mathbf{e}_{4}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="fill:none" d="M 382.78 -130.72"></path><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 384.34 -138.42)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.98em;--ltx-fo-height:0.44em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" height="8.23" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 6.15)" width="13.5"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S1.F1.pic1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\displaystyle\mathbf{e}_{6}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle\mathbf{e}_{6}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="fill:none" d="M 311.24 -167.92"></path><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 312.8 -175.63)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.98em;--ltx-fo-height:0.44em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" height="8.23" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 6.15)" width="13.5"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S1.F1.pic1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\displaystyle\mathbf{e}_{5}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle\mathbf{e}_{5}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="fill:none" d="M 192.76 -90.04"></path><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 194.31 -98.74)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.35em;--ltx-fo-height:0.44em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:11.75pt;" height="7.15" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.15)" width="5.75"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S1.F1.pic1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\iota" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="1.200em">ι</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iota</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="fill:none" d="M 42.74 -197.65"></path><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 44.29 -209.59)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:2.49em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="34.44"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S1.F1.pic1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(A,\rho)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(A,\rho)</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="fill:none" d="M 286.21 -195.46"></path><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 287.76 -208.28)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:4.83em;--ltx-fo-height:0.81em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.29em;font-size:10pt;" height="15.22" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 11.26)" width="66.89"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S1.F1.pic1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(\mathbb{P}\left(\mathbb{C}^{6}\right),d_{p}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mn>6</mn></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(\mathbb{P}\left(\mathbb{C}^{6}\right),d_{p}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="fill:none" d="M 302.91 -87.99"></path><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 304.46 -95.7)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.98em;--ltx-fo-height:0.44em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" height="8.23" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 6.15)" width="13.5"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S1.F1.pic1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\displaystyle\mathbf{e}_{3}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle\mathbf{e}_{3}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="fill:none" d="M 57.74 -87.99"></path><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 59.3 -95.51)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.98em;--ltx-fo-height:0.43em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" height="8.03" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 5.96)" width="13.52"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S1.F1.pic1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\displaystyle\mathnormal{a}_{3}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle\mathnormal{a}_{3}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S1.F1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 1</span>: </span><span id="S1.F1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">An illustration of Remark <a href="#ThmThm5" title="Remark 5. ‣ 1 Introduction and main result ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> (for <math id="S1.F1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=6</annotation></semantics></math>). Given any <math id="S1.F1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>-element metric space <math id="S1.F1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(A,\rho)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(A,\rho)</annotation></semantics></math>, we can isometrically embed it into <math id="S1.F1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathbb{P}(\mathbb{C}^{n}),d_{p})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathbb{P}(\mathbb{C}^{n}),d_{p})</annotation></semantics></math> with the distance function <math id="S1.F1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> defined via (<a href="#S1.E3" title="In 1 Introduction and main result ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>) for any chosen <math id="S1.F1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>. In doing so, the elements <math id="S1.F1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S1.F1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> are promoted to the orthonormal basis states <math id="S1.F1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{e}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{e}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> (defined up to a phase factor). Loosely speaking, the above construction provides a general way to ‘quantize’ any finite metric space.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="ThmThm5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_Rem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="ThmThm5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 5</span></span><span id="ThmThm5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="ThmThm5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="ThmThm5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The result that <math id="ThmThm5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> is a true distance function can be seen as providing a way to isometrically embed any <math id="ThmThm5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>-element metric space into the space of pure quantum states ‘spanned’ upon its elements (cf. Fig. <a href="#S1.F1" title="Figure 1 ‣ 1 Introduction and main result ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>). More concretely, given a finite metric space <math id="ThmThm5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(A,\rho)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(A,\rho)</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="ThmThm5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\vcentcolon=\{a_{1},\ldots,a_{n}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\vcentcolon=\{a_{1},\ldots,a_{n}\}</annotation></semantics></math> and the associated distance matrix <math id="ThmThm5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{ij}\vcentcolon=\rho(a_{i},a_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{ij}\vcentcolon=\rho(a_{i},a_{j})</annotation></semantics></math>, the map <math id="ThmThm5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\iota:A\rightarrow\mathbb{P}(\mathbb{C}^{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ι</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iota:A\rightarrow\mathbb{P}(\mathbb{C}^{n})</annotation></semantics></math> defined via <math id="ThmThm5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\iota(a_{i})\vcentcolon=\mathbf{e}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ι</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iota(a_{i})\vcentcolon=\mathbf{e}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> (modulo phase factor) is an <em id="ThmThm5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">isometric embedding</em> of <math id="ThmThm5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(A,\rho)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(A,\rho)</annotation></semantics></math> into <math id="ThmThm5.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathbb{P}(\mathbb{C}^{n}),d_{p})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathbb{P}(\mathbb{C}^{n}),d_{p})</annotation></semantics></math>, because clearly</p>
<table id="S1.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S1.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S1.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle d_{p}(\iota(a_{i}),\iota(a_{j}))=d_{p}(\mathbf{e}_{i},\mathbf{e}_{j})=E_{ij}=\rho(a_{i},a_{j})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ι</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>ι</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle d_{p}(\iota(a_{i}),\iota(a_{j}))=d_{p}(\mathbf{e}_{i},\mathbf{e}_{j})=E_{ij}=\rho(a_{i},a_{j}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="ThmThm6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_Rem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="ThmThm6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 6</span></span><span id="ThmThm6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="ThmThm6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="ThmThm6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Although the elements of <math id="ThmThm6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(\mathbb{C}^{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(\mathbb{C}^{n})</annotation></semantics></math>, when regarded as norm-one vectors from <math id="ThmThm6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{C}}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{C}}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, are defined up to a phase factor, we can—and will—forget about the latter cumbersome fact while proving (<a href="#S1.E4" title="In Theorem 2. ‣ 1 Introduction and main result ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>). In other words, from now on our aim is to prove that the triangle inequality (<a href="#S1.E4" title="In Theorem 2. ‣ 1 Introduction and main result ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>) holds for any <math id="ThmThm6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textup{{x}},\textup{{y}},\textup{{z}}\in{\mathbb{C}}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo>,</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textup{{x}},\textup{{y}},\textup{{z}}\in{\mathbb{C}}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="ThmThm6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\textup{{x}}\|=\|\textup{{y}}\|=\|\textup{{z}}\|=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\textup{{x}}\|=\|\textup{{y}}\|=\|\textup{{z}}\|=1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p9.1" class="ltx_p">Theorem <a href="#ThmThm2" title="Theorem 2. ‣ 1 Introduction and main result ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> has important implications. It solidifies the theoretical foundation for using the distances <math id="S1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> in rigorous applications across quantum information science. Furthermore, it fully establishes (<a href="#S1.E3" title="In 1 Introduction and main result ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>) as <em id="S1.p9.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">the</em> way of inducing a metric space structure on <math id="S1.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(\mathbb{C}^{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(\mathbb{C}^{n})</annotation></semantics></math> by a given distance matrix. Finally, since <math id="S1.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#S1.E3" title="In 1 Introduction and main result ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>) is arbitrary, <math id="S1.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> can be understood as the pure-state version of the quantum Wasserstein distance of order <math id="S1.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>]</cite>, extending the implications of the presented results.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p10.1" class="ltx_p">The paper is self-contained and its outline is as follows. In Section <a href="#S2" title="2 The 𝑛=3 case and its consequences ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> we prove Theorem <a href="#ThmThm2" title="Theorem 2. ‣ 1 Introduction and main result ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> for the first nontrivial case <math id="S1.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=3</annotation></semantics></math> (Proposition <a href="#ThmThm7" title="Proposition 7. ‣ 2 The 𝑛=3 case and its consequences ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>) and later demonstrate that for <math id="S1.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n&gt;3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n&gt;3</annotation></semantics></math> it is enough to prove (<a href="#S1.E4" title="In Theorem 2. ‣ 1 Introduction and main result ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>) for <math id="S1.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\textup{{x}},\textup{{y}},\textup{{z}}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\textup{{x}},\textup{{y}},\textup{{z}}\}</annotation></semantics></math> <em id="S1.p10.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">orthonormal</em> (Proposition <a href="#ThmThm8" title="Proposition 8. ‣ 2 The 𝑛=3 case and its consequences ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>). Then, in Section <a href="#S3" title="3 A certain convexity result and the proof of the triangle inequality ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> we show precisely that by first establishing a certain non-trivial convexity result (Theorem <a href="#ThmThm9" title="Theorem 9. ‣ 3 A certain convexity result and the proof of the triangle inequality ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">2 </span>The <math id="S2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=3</annotation></semantics></math> case and its consequences</h2>

<div id="S2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Just as announced in Remark <a href="#ThmThm6" title="Remark 6. ‣ 1 Introduction and main result ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>, in what follows we will regard <math id="S2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> as defined on the (pairs of) norm-one vectors, and not their equivalence classes modulo phase factor. For <math id="S2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=3</annotation></semantics></math>, this in particular means that definition (<a href="#S1.E3" title="In 1 Introduction and main result ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>) can be written with the help of the cross product as <math id="S2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{p}(\textup{{x}},\textup{{y}})=\|\textup{{E}}^{p/2}(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{y}})\|^{2/p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">E</mtext><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{p}(\textup{{x}},\textup{{y}})=\|\textup{{E}}^{p/2}(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{y}})\|^{2/p}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textup{{E}}=\diag(E_{23},E_{13},E_{12})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">E</mtext><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>23</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>13</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>12</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textup{{E}}=\diag(E_{23},E_{13},E_{12})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For later use, let us recall some basic identities involving the cross product (valid for any <math id="S2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{C}}^{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{C}}^{3}</annotation></semantics></math> vectors, not just those of norm 1):</p>
<table id="S2.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.E5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\textup{{x}}^{\top}(\textup{{y}}\times\textup{{z}})=\textup{{y}}^{\top}(\textup{{z}}\times\textup{{x}})=\textup{{z}}^{\top}(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{y}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\textup{{x}}^{\top}(\textup{{y}}\times\textup{{z}})=\textup{{y}}^{\top}(\textup{{z}}\times\textup{{x}})=\textup{{z}}^{\top}(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{y}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.E6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{y}})^{\top}(\textup{{z}}\times\mathbf{u})=(\textup{{x}}^{\top}\textup{{z}})(\textup{{y}}^{\top}\mathbf{u})-(\textup{{x}}^{\top}\mathbf{u})(\textup{{y}}^{\top}\textup{{z}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>𝐮</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐮</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐮</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{y}})^{\top}(\textup{{z}}\times\mathbf{u})=(\textup{{x}}^{\top}\textup{{z}})(\textup{{y}}^{\top}\mathbf{u})-(\textup{{x}}^{\top}\mathbf{u})(\textup{{y}}^{\top}\textup{{z}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.E7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\textup{{x}}\times(\textup{{y}}\times\textup{{z}})=(\textup{{x}}^{\top}\textup{{z}})\textup{{y}}-(\textup{{x}}^{\top}\textup{{y}})\textup{{z}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\textup{{x}}\times(\textup{{y}}\times\textup{{z}})=(\textup{{x}}^{\top}\textup{{z}})\textup{{y}}-(\textup{{x}}^{\top}\textup{{y}})\textup{{z}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.E8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{z}})\times(\textup{{y}}\times\textup{{z}})=(\textup{{z}}^{\top}(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{y}}))\textup{{z}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{z}})\times(\textup{{y}}\times\textup{{z}})=(\textup{{z}}^{\top}(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{y}}))\textup{{z}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.E9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{A}\textup{{x}}\times\mathbf{A}\textup{{y}}=(\cof\mathbf{A})(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{y}}),\qquad\mathbf{A}\in\textup{GL}({\mathbb{C}}^{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>𝐀</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>cof</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>𝐀</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mtext>GL</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{A}\textup{{x}}\times\mathbf{A}\textup{{y}}=(\cof\mathbf{A})(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{y}}),\qquad\mathbf{A}\in\textup{GL}({\mathbb{C}}^{3})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\cof\mathbf{A}=(\det\mathbf{A})(\mathbf{A}^{-1})^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>cof</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>𝐀</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mi>𝐀</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐀</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cof\mathbf{A}=(\det\mathbf{A})(\mathbf{A}^{-1})^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>. Identity (<a href="#S2.E6" title="In 2 The 𝑛=3 case and its consequences ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>) in particular implies that<span id="footnote3" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">3</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">3</sup>
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">3</span>
            
            
            
          Identity (<a href="#S2.E10" title="In 2 The 𝑛=3 case and its consequences ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>) can be also viewed as the special case of the Lagrange identity.</span></span></span></p>
<table id="S2.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.E10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{y}}\|^{2}=\|\textup{{x}}\|^{2}\|\textup{{y}}\|^{2}-|\textup{{x}}^{\dagger}\textup{{y}}|^{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{y}}\|^{2}=\|\textup{{x}}\|^{2}\|\textup{{y}}\|^{2}-|\textup{{x}}^{\dagger}\textup{{y}}|^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p2.3" class="ltx_p">which in turn implies that <math id="S2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{y}}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{y}}=0</annotation></semantics></math> if and only if <math id="S2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textup{{x}}=c\textup{{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textup{{x}}=c\textup{{y}}</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="S2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\in{\mathbb{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℂ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\in{\mathbb{C}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The following simple fact will also turn out to be important,</p>
<table id="S2.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.E11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\RE(\textup{{x}}^{\dagger}\textup{{y}})=\RE\textup{{x}}^{\top}\RE\textup{{y}}+\IM\textup{{x}}^{\top}\IM\textup{{y}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Re</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Im</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\RE(\textup{{x}}^{\dagger}\textup{{y}})=\RE\textup{{x}}^{\top}\RE\textup{{y}}+\IM\textup{{x}}^{\top}\IM\textup{{y}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The main result of this section is as follows.</p>
</div>
<div id="ThmThm7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_Prop">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="ThmThm7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 7</span></span><span id="ThmThm7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="ThmThm7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="ThmThm7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="ThmThm7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix any <math id="ThmThm7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math> and any positive-definite <math id="ThmThm7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textup{{E}}\in\textup{GL}({\mathbb{C}}^{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">E</mtext><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mtext>GL</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textup{{E}}\in\textup{GL}({\mathbb{C}}^{3})</annotation></semantics></math>. The triangle inequality</span></p>
<table id="S2.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.E12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\textup{{E}}^{p/2}(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{y}})\|^{2/p}\leq\|\textup{{E}}^{p/2}(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{z}})\|^{2/p}+\|\textup{{E}}^{p/2}(\textup{{y}}\times\textup{{z}})\|^{2/p},\quad\|\textup{{x}}\|=\|\textup{{y}}\|=\|\textup{{z}}\|=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">E</mtext><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">E</mtext><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">E</mtext><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\textup{{E}}^{p/2}(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{y}})\|^{2/p}\leq\|\textup{{E}}^{p/2}(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{z}})\|^{2/p}+\|\textup{{E}}^{p/2}(\textup{{y}}\times\textup{{z}})\|^{2/p},\quad\|\textup{{x}}\|=\|\textup{{y}}\|=\|\textup{{z}}\|=1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="ThmThm7.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="ThmThm7.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">holds if and only if the spectral radius <math id="ThmThm7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho(\textup{{E}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">E</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho(\textup{{E}})</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies<span id="footnote4" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">4</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">4</sup>
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note"><span id="footnote4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">4</span></span>
                
                
                
              <span id="footnote4.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">For </span><span id="footnote4.7" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_bold ltx_font_upright">E</span><span id="footnote4.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright"> positive-definite, condition (</span><a href="#S2.E13" title="In Proposition 7. ‣ 2 The 𝑛=3 case and its consequences ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_upright"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a><span id="footnote4.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">) is equivalent to the triangle inequality for its eigenvalues. Note that instead of </span><math id="footnote4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho(\textup{{E}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">E</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho(\textup{{E}})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="footnote4.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright"> one can equally well use the spectral norm </span><math id="footnote4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\textup{{E}}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">E</mtext><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\textup{{E}}\|</annotation></semantics></math><span id="footnote4.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright"> or the numerical radius </span><math id="footnote4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(\textup{{E}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">E</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(\textup{{E}})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="footnote4.12" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">.</span></span></span></span></span></p>
<table id="S2.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.E13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 2\rho(\textup{{E}})\leq\tr\textup{{E}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">E</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">E</mtext></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 2\rho(\textup{{E}})\leq\tr\textup{{E}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Without loss of generality, we may regard <span id="S2.p5.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_bold">E</span> as a diagonal matrix, because for any unitary matrix <math id="S2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐔</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{U}</annotation></semantics></math>, on the strength of (<a href="#S2.E9" title="In 2 The 𝑛=3 case and its consequences ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>),</span></p>
<table id="S2.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\textup{{E}}^{p/2}(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{y}})\|=\|\mathbf{U}^{\dagger}\textup{{E}}^{p/2}\mathbf{U}\mathbf{U}^{\dagger}(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{y}})\|=\|(\mathbf{U}^{\dagger}\textup{{E}}\mathbf{U})^{p/2}(\mathbf{U}^{\top}\textup{{x}}\times\mathbf{U}^{\top}\textup{{y}})\|," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">E</mtext><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐔</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">E</mtext><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐔𝐔</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐔</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">E</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐔</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝐔</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>𝐔</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\textup{{E}}^{p/2}(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{y}})\|=\|\mathbf{U}^{\dagger}\textup{{E}}^{p/2}\mathbf{U}\mathbf{U}^{\dagger}(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{y}})\|=\|(\mathbf{U}^{\dagger}\textup{{E}}\mathbf{U})^{p/2}(\mathbf{U}^{\top}\textup{{x}}\times\mathbf{U}^{\top}\textup{{y}})\|,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">so <span id="S2.p5.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_bold">E</span> can always be diagonalized. Of course, condition (<a href="#S2.E13" title="In Proposition 7. ‣ 2 The 𝑛=3 case and its consequences ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>) is invariant under unitary rotations.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">From now on we thus assume that <math id="S2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textup{{E}}=\textup{diag}(\lambda_{1},\lambda_{2},\lambda_{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">E</mtext><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>diag</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textup{{E}}=\textup{diag}(\lambda_{1},\lambda_{2},\lambda_{3})</annotation></semantics></math> (with <math id="S2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{i}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{i}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.) Verifying the necessity of condition (<a href="#S2.E13" title="In Proposition 7. ‣ 2 The 𝑛=3 case and its consequences ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>) is easy. Plugging the canonical basis <math id="S2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textup{{x}}=\mathbf{e}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textup{{x}}=\mathbf{e}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textup{{y}}=\mathbf{e}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textup{{y}}=\mathbf{e}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textup{{z}}=\mathbf{e}_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textup{{z}}=\mathbf{e}_{3}</annotation></semantics></math> into (<a href="#S2.E12" title="In Proposition 7. ‣ 2 The 𝑛=3 case and its consequences ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>) yields <math id="S2.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{3}\leq\lambda_{2}+\lambda_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{3}\leq\lambda_{2}+\lambda_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and permuting the indices gives the other two inequalities. Altogether, this yields <math id="S2.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\max_{i}\lambda_{i}\leq\lambda_{1}+\lambda_{2}+\lambda_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\max_{i}\lambda_{i}\leq\lambda_{1}+\lambda_{2}+\lambda_{3}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is nothing but (<a href="#S2.E13" title="In Proposition 7. ‣ 2 The 𝑛=3 case and its consequences ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Proving the sufficiency of (<a href="#S2.E13" title="In Proposition 7. ‣ 2 The 𝑛=3 case and its consequences ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>), however, is much more complicated. The idea is to minimize the function <math id="S2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\textup{{E}}^{p/2}(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{z}})\|^{2/p}+\|\textup{{E}}^{p/2}(\textup{{z}}\times\textup{{y}})\|^{2/p}-\|\textup{{E}}^{p/2}(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{y}})\|^{2/p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">E</mtext><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">E</mtext><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">E</mtext><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\textup{{E}}^{p/2}(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{z}})\|^{2/p}+\|\textup{{E}}^{p/2}(\textup{{z}}\times\textup{{y}})\|^{2/p}-\|\textup{{E}}^{p/2}(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{y}})\|^{2/p}</annotation></semantics></math> subject to the constraints <math id="S2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\textup{{x}}\|=\|\textup{{y}}\|=\|\textup{{z}}\|=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\textup{{x}}\|=\|\textup{{y}}\|=\|\textup{{z}}\|=1</annotation></semantics></math> using the method of Lagrange multipliers.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Concretely, let us denote <math id="S2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{M}\vcentcolon=\textup{{E}}^{p/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐌</mi><mo>:=</mo><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">E</mtext><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{M}\vcentcolon=\textup{{E}}^{p/2}</annotation></semantics></math> and consider the function <math id="S2.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L:{\mathbb{C}}^{3}\times{\mathbb{C}}^{3}\times{\mathbb{C}}^{3}\times{\mathbb{R}}^{3}\cong{\mathbb{R}}^{21}\rightarrow{\mathbb{R}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≅</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mn>21</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L:{\mathbb{C}}^{3}\times{\mathbb{C}}^{3}\times{\mathbb{C}}^{3}\times{\mathbb{R}}^{3}\cong{\mathbb{R}}^{21}\rightarrow{\mathbb{R}}</annotation></semantics></math> defined as</span></p>
<table id="S2.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle L(\textup{{x}},\textup{{y}},\textup{{z}};\alpha,\beta,\gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle L(\textup{{x}},\textup{{y}},\textup{{z}};\alpha,\beta,\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\|\mathbf{M}(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{z}})\|^{2/p}+\|\mathbf{M}(\textup{{y}}\times\textup{{z}})\|^{2/p}-\|\mathbf{M}(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{y}})\|^{2/p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐌</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐌</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐌</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\|\mathbf{M}(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{z}})\|^{2/p}+\|\mathbf{M}(\textup{{y}}\times\textup{{z}})\|^{2/p}-\|\mathbf{M}(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{y}})\|^{2/p}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\tfrac{1}{p}\alpha(\|\textup{{x}}\|^{2}-1)-\tfrac{1}{p}\beta(\|\textup{{y}}\|^{2}-1)-\tfrac{1}{p}\gamma(\|\textup{{z}}\|^{2}-1)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>p</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>p</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>p</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\tfrac{1}{p}\alpha(\|\textup{{x}}\|^{2}-1)-\tfrac{1}{p}\beta(\|\textup{{y}}\|^{2}-1)-\tfrac{1}{p}\gamma(\|\textup{{z}}\|^{2}-1).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">We are interested in finding its stationary points as well as points of non-differentiability, because only at those points <math id="S2.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> can attain global minimum (subject to our constraints).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">The points of non-differentiability belonging to the feasible set are exactly those for which either</span></p>
<ul id="S2.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{z}}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{z}}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, but then for <math id="S2.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\textup{{x}}\|=\|\textup{{z}}\|=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\textup{{x}}\|=\|\textup{{z}}\|=1</annotation></semantics></math> we must have <math id="S2.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textup{{z}}=\textup{e}^{\textup{i}\phi}\textup{{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mtext>e</mtext><mrow><mtext>i</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textup{{z}}=\textup{e}^{\textup{i}\phi}\textup{{x}}</annotation></semantics></math> and so (<a href="#S2.E12" title="In Proposition 7. ‣ 2 The 𝑛=3 case and its consequences ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>) holds as an equality;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S2.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textup{{y}}\times\textup{{z}}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textup{{y}}\times\textup{{z}}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, but then we similarly obtain that <math id="S2.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textup{{z}}=\textup{e}^{\textup{i}\phi}\textup{{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mtext>e</mtext><mrow><mtext>i</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textup{{z}}=\textup{e}^{\textup{i}\phi}\textup{{y}}</annotation></semantics></math> and (<a href="#S2.E12" title="In Proposition 7. ‣ 2 The 𝑛=3 case and its consequences ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>) holds as an equality;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S2.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S2.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{y}}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{y}}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, but then the LHS in (<a href="#S2.E12" title="In Proposition 7. ‣ 2 The 𝑛=3 case and its consequences ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>) is zero.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="S2.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">Having taken care of the points of non-differentiability, we can from now on assume that <math id="S2.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{y}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{z}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{z}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textup{{y}}\times\textup{{z}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textup{{y}}\times\textup{{z}}</annotation></semantics></math> are all nonzero and calculate the total derivative <math id="S2.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textup{d}L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>d</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textup{d}L</annotation></semantics></math> term by term. Denoting <math id="S2.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{13}\vcentcolon=\|\mathbf{M}(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{z}})\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>13</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐌</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{13}\vcentcolon=\|\mathbf{M}(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{z}})\|</annotation></semantics></math>, one obtains, for instance,</span></p>
<table id="S2.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\textup{d}\|\mathbf{M}(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{z}})\|^{2/p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>d</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐌</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\textup{d}\|\mathbf{M}(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{z}})\|^{2/p}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{pM_{13}^{2(p-1)/p}}\textup{d}((\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{z}})^{\dagger}\mathbf{M}^{2}(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{z}}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mn>13</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>d</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐌</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{pM_{13}^{2(p-1)/p}}\textup{d}((\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{z}})^{\dagger}\mathbf{M}^{2}(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{z}}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{2}{pM_{13}^{2(p-1)/p}}\RE\left[(\mathbf{M}^{2}(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{z}}))^{\dagger}(\textup{d}\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{z}}+\textup{{x}}\times\textup{d}\textup{{z}})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mn>13</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐌</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>d</mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mtext>d</mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{2}{pM_{13}^{2(p-1)/p}}\RE\left[(\mathbf{M}^{2}(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{z}}))^{\dagger}(\textup{d}\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{z}}+\textup{{x}}\times\textup{d}\textup{{z}})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{2}{pM_{13}^{2(p-1)/p}}\Big(\RE\Big[(\bar{\textup{{z}}}\times\mathbf{M}^{2}(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{z}}))^{\dagger}\textup{d}\textup{{x}}\Big]-\RE\Big[(\bar{\textup{{x}}}\times\mathbf{M}^{2}(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{z}}))^{\dagger}\textup{d}\textup{{z}}\Big]\Big)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mn>13</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>𝐌</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mtext>d</mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>𝐌</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mtext>d</mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{2}{pM_{13}^{2(p-1)/p}}\Big(\RE\Big[(\bar{\textup{{z}}}\times\mathbf{M}^{2}(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{z}}))^{\dagger}\textup{d}\textup{{x}}\Big]-\RE\Big[(\bar{\textup{{x}}}\times\mathbf{M}^{2}(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{z}}))^{\dagger}\textup{d}\textup{{z}}\Big]\Big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text">where in the last equality we have used (<a href="#S2.E5" title="In 2 The 𝑛=3 case and its consequences ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>). Calculating <math id="S2.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textup{d}\|\mathbf{M}(\textup{{y}}\times\textup{{z}})\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>d</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐌</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textup{d}\|\mathbf{M}(\textup{{y}}\times\textup{{z}})\|</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textup{d}\|\mathbf{M}(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{y}})\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>d</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐌</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textup{d}\|\mathbf{M}(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{y}})\|</annotation></semantics></math> similarly, along with the total derivatives of the Lagrange multipliers terms, such as</span></p>
<table id="S2.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\textup{d}\left(\tfrac{1}{p}\alpha(\|\textup{{x}}\|^{2}-1)\right)=\tfrac{2}{p}\alpha\RE(\textup{{x}}^{\dagger}\textup{d}\textup{{x}})+\tfrac{1}{p}(\|\textup{{x}}\|^{2}-1)\textup{d}\alpha," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>d</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>p</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>p</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mtext>d</mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>p</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>d</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\textup{d}\left(\tfrac{1}{p}\alpha(\|\textup{{x}}\|^{2}-1)\right)=\tfrac{2}{p}\alpha\RE(\textup{{x}}^{\dagger}\textup{d}\textup{{x}})+\tfrac{1}{p}(\|\textup{{x}}\|^{2}-1)\textup{d}\alpha,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p10.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p10.3.1" class="ltx_text">one arrives at <math id="S2.p10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textup{d}L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>d</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textup{d}L</annotation></semantics></math> of the following form</span></p>
<table id="S2.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{p}{2}\textup{d}L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>d</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{p}{2}\textup{d}L</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\RE\Bigg[\left(\frac{\bar{\textup{{z}}}\times\mathbf{M}^{2}(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{z}})}{M_{13}^{2(p-1)/p}}-\frac{\bar{\textup{{y}}}\times\mathbf{M}^{2}(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{y}})}{M_{12}^{2(p-1)/p}}-\alpha\textup{{x}}\right)^{\dagger}\textup{d}\textup{{x}}\Bigg]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>𝐌</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mn>13</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>𝐌</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mn>12</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mtext>d</mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\RE\Bigg[\left(\frac{\bar{\textup{{z}}}\times\mathbf{M}^{2}(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{z}})}{M_{13}^{2(p-1)/p}}-\frac{\bar{\textup{{y}}}\times\mathbf{M}^{2}(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{y}})}{M_{12}^{2(p-1)/p}}-\alpha\textup{{x}}\right)^{\dagger}\textup{d}\textup{{x}}\Bigg]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\RE{\Bigg[}\left(\frac{\bar{\textup{{z}}}\times\mathbf{M}^{2}(\textup{{y}}\times\textup{{z}})}{M_{23}^{2(p-1)/p}}+\frac{\bar{\textup{{x}}}\times\mathbf{M}^{2}(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{y}})}{M_{12}^{2(p-1)/p}}-\beta\textup{{y}}\right)^{\dagger}\textup{d}\textup{{y}}\Bigg]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">+</mo><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>𝐌</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mn>23</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>𝐌</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mn>12</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mtext>d</mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\RE{\Bigg[}\left(\frac{\bar{\textup{{z}}}\times\mathbf{M}^{2}(\textup{{y}}\times\textup{{z}})}{M_{23}^{2(p-1)/p}}+\frac{\bar{\textup{{x}}}\times\mathbf{M}^{2}(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{y}})}{M_{12}^{2(p-1)/p}}-\beta\textup{{y}}\right)^{\dagger}\textup{d}\textup{{y}}\Bigg]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\RE\Bigg[\left(-\frac{\bar{\textup{{x}}}\times\mathbf{M}^{2}(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{z}})}{M_{13}^{2(p-1)/p}}-\frac{\bar{\textup{{y}}}\times\mathbf{M}^{2}(\textup{{y}}\times\textup{{z}})}{M_{23}^{2(p-1)/p}}-\gamma\textup{{z}}\right)^{\dagger}\textup{d}\textup{{z}}\Bigg]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">+</mo><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>𝐌</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mn>13</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>𝐌</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mn>23</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mtext>d</mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\RE\Bigg[\left(-\frac{\bar{\textup{{x}}}\times\mathbf{M}^{2}(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{z}})}{M_{13}^{2(p-1)/p}}-\frac{\bar{\textup{{y}}}\times\mathbf{M}^{2}(\textup{{y}}\times\textup{{z}})}{M_{23}^{2(p-1)/p}}-\gamma\textup{{z}}\right)^{\dagger}\textup{d}\textup{{z}}\Bigg]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\tfrac{1}{2}(\|\textup{{x}}\|^{2}-1)\textup{d}\alpha-\tfrac{1}{2}(\|\textup{{y}}\|^{2}-1)\textup{d}\beta-\tfrac{1}{2}(\|\textup{{z}}\|^{2}-1)\textup{d}\gamma," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>d</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>d</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>d</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\tfrac{1}{2}(\|\textup{{x}}\|^{2}-1)\textup{d}\alpha-\tfrac{1}{2}(\|\textup{{y}}\|^{2}-1)\textup{d}\beta-\tfrac{1}{2}(\|\textup{{z}}\|^{2}-1)\textup{d}\gamma,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p10.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p10.4.1" class="ltx_text">where we have denoted <math id="S2.p10.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{12}\vcentcolon=\|\mathbf{M}(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{y}})\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>12</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐌</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{12}\vcentcolon=\|\mathbf{M}(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{y}})\|</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.p10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{13}\vcentcolon=\|\mathbf{M}(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{z}})\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>13</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐌</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{13}\vcentcolon=\|\mathbf{M}(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{z}})\|</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.p10.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{23}\vcentcolon=\|\mathbf{M}(\textup{{y}}\times\textup{{z}})\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>23</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐌</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{23}\vcentcolon=\|\mathbf{M}(\textup{{y}}\times\textup{{z}})\|</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">The method of Lagrange multipliers works for functions of <em id="S2.p11.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">real</em> variables and formally <math id="S2.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> is a function of the <em id="S2.p11.1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">six real 3-vectors</em>: <math id="S2.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\RE\textup{{x}},\IM\textup{{x}},\RE\textup{{y}},\IM\textup{{y}},\RE\textup{{z}},\IM\textup{{z}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\RE\textup{{x}},\IM\textup{{x}},\RE\textup{{y}},\IM\textup{{y}},\RE\textup{{z}},\IM\textup{{z}}</annotation></semantics></math> (along with <math id="S2.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>). Luckily, if we now apply (<a href="#S2.E11" title="In 2 The 𝑛=3 case and its consequences ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>), the differentials of these real 3-vectors (i.e. <math id="S2.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textup{d}\RE\textup{{x}}=\RE\textup{d}\textup{{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>d</mtext><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mtext>d</mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textup{d}\RE\textup{{x}}=\RE\textup{d}\textup{{x}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.p11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textup{d}\IM\textup{{x}}=\IM\textup{d}\textup{{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>d</mtext><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mtext>d</mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textup{d}\IM\textup{{x}}=\IM\textup{d}\textup{{x}}</annotation></semantics></math>, etc.) all explicitly appear—next to the real and imaginary parts of the complex 3-vectors in the big round brackets above. Vanishing of all the first partial derivatives can be thus expressed as the following system of three complex vector equations + the three original constraints:</span></p>
<table id="S2.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.EGx14.1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.EGx14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\{\begin{array}[]{l}\alpha\textup{{x}}=\frac{\bar{\textup{{z}}}\times\mathbf{M}^{2}(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{z}})}{M_{13}^{2(p-1)/p}}-\frac{\bar{\textup{{y}}}\times\mathbf{M}^{2}(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{y}})}{M_{12}^{2(p-1)/p}}\\[8.0pt]
\beta\textup{{y}}=\frac{\bar{\textup{{z}}}\times\mathbf{M}^{2}(\textup{{y}}\times\textup{{z}})}{M_{23}^{2(p-1)/p}}+\frac{\bar{\textup{{x}}}\times\mathbf{M}^{2}(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{y}})}{M_{12}^{2(p-1)/p}}\\[8.0pt]
\gamma\textup{{z}}=-\frac{\bar{\textup{{x}}}\times\mathbf{M}^{2}(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{z}})}{M_{13}^{2(p-1)/p}}-\frac{\bar{\textup{{y}}}\times\mathbf{M}^{2}(\textup{{y}}\times\textup{{z}})}{M_{23}^{2(p-1)/p}}\\[8.0pt]
\|\textup{{x}}\|=\|\textup{{y}}\|=\|\textup{{z}}\|=1\end{array}\right." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>𝐌</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mn>13</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>𝐌</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mn>12</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>𝐌</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mn>23</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>𝐌</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mn>12</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>𝐌</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mn>13</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup></mfrac></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>𝐌</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mn>23</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\{\begin{array}[]{l}\alpha\textup{{x}}=\frac{\bar{\textup{{z}}}\times\mathbf{M}^{2}(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{z}})}{M_{13}^{2(p-1)/p}}-\frac{\bar{\textup{{y}}}\times\mathbf{M}^{2}(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{y}})}{M_{12}^{2(p-1)/p}}\\[8.0pt]
\beta\textup{{y}}=\frac{\bar{\textup{{z}}}\times\mathbf{M}^{2}(\textup{{y}}\times\textup{{z}})}{M_{23}^{2(p-1)/p}}+\frac{\bar{\textup{{x}}}\times\mathbf{M}^{2}(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{y}})}{M_{12}^{2(p-1)/p}}\\[8.0pt]
\gamma\textup{{z}}=-\frac{\bar{\textup{{x}}}\times\mathbf{M}^{2}(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{z}})}{M_{13}^{2(p-1)/p}}-\frac{\bar{\textup{{y}}}\times\mathbf{M}^{2}(\textup{{y}}\times\textup{{z}})}{M_{23}^{2(p-1)/p}}\\[8.0pt]
\|\textup{{x}}\|=\|\textup{{y}}\|=\|\textup{{z}}\|=1\end{array}\right.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S2.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">In order to extract some information from equations (<a href="#S2.EGx14" title="Proof. ‣ 2 The 𝑛=3 case and its consequences ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>), let us take their inner products with <span id="S2.p12.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_bold">x</span>, <span id="S2.p12.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_bold">y</span>, <span id="S2.p12.1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_bold">z</span>, obtaining</span></p>
<table id="S2.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.E18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\alpha=M_{13}^{2/p}-M_{12}^{2/p},\quad\beta=M_{23}^{2/p}-M_{12}^{2/p},\quad\gamma=M_{13}^{2/p}+M_{23}^{2/p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mn>13</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mn>12</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mn>23</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mn>12</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mn>13</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mn>23</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\alpha=M_{13}^{2/p}-M_{12}^{2/p},\quad\beta=M_{23}^{2/p}-M_{12}^{2/p},\quad\gamma=M_{13}^{2/p}+M_{23}^{2/p}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p12.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p12.2.1" class="ltx_text">along with</span></p>
<table id="S2.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\alpha\textup{{y}}^{\dagger}\textup{{x}}=\frac{(\textup{{y}}\times\textup{{z}})^{\dagger}\mathbf{M}^{2}(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{z}})}{M_{13}^{2(p-1)/p}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐌</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mn>13</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\alpha\textup{{y}}^{\dagger}\textup{{x}}=\frac{(\textup{{y}}\times\textup{{z}})^{\dagger}\mathbf{M}^{2}(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{z}})}{M_{13}^{2(p-1)/p}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\beta\textup{{x}}^{\dagger}\textup{{y}}=\frac{(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{z}})^{\dagger}\mathbf{M}^{2}(\textup{{y}}\times\textup{{z}})}{M_{23}^{2(p-1)/p}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐌</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mn>23</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\beta\textup{{x}}^{\dagger}\textup{{y}}=\frac{(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{z}})^{\dagger}\mathbf{M}^{2}(\textup{{y}}\times\textup{{z}})}{M_{23}^{2(p-1)/p}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\gamma\textup{{x}}^{\dagger}\textup{{z}}=-\frac{(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{y}})^{\dagger}\mathbf{M}^{2}(\textup{{y}}\times\textup{{z}})}{M_{23}^{2(p-1)/p}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐌</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mn>23</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\gamma\textup{{x}}^{\dagger}\textup{{z}}=-\frac{(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{y}})^{\dagger}\mathbf{M}^{2}(\textup{{y}}\times\textup{{z}})}{M_{23}^{2(p-1)/p}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\alpha\textup{{z}}^{\dagger}\textup{{x}}=\frac{(\textup{{y}}\times\textup{{z}})^{\dagger}\mathbf{M}^{2}(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{y}})}{M_{12}^{2(p-1)/p}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐌</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mn>12</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\alpha\textup{{z}}^{\dagger}\textup{{x}}=\frac{(\textup{{y}}\times\textup{{z}})^{\dagger}\mathbf{M}^{2}(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{y}})}{M_{12}^{2(p-1)/p}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\beta\textup{{z}}^{\dagger}\textup{{y}}=-\frac{(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{z}})^{\dagger}\mathbf{M}^{2}(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{y}})}{M_{12}^{2(p-1)/p}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐌</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mn>12</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\beta\textup{{z}}^{\dagger}\textup{{y}}=-\frac{(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{z}})^{\dagger}\mathbf{M}^{2}(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{y}})}{M_{12}^{2(p-1)/p}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\gamma\textup{{y}}^{\dagger}\textup{{z}}=\frac{(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{y}})^{\dagger}\mathbf{M}^{2}(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{z}})}{M_{13}^{2(p-1)/p}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐌</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mn>13</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\gamma\textup{{y}}^{\dagger}\textup{{z}}=\frac{(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{y}})^{\dagger}\mathbf{M}^{2}(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{z}})}{M_{13}^{2(p-1)/p}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p12.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p12.3.1" class="ltx_text">We have the following implications.</span></p>
<ul id="S2.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S2.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S2.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="S2.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textup{{x}}^{\dagger}\textup{{y}}\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textup{{x}}^{\dagger}\textup{{y}}\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S2.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha M_{13}^{2(p-1)/p}=\beta M_{23}^{2(p-1)/p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mn>13</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mn>23</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha M_{13}^{2(p-1)/p}=\beta M_{23}^{2(p-1)/p}</annotation></semantics></math>, which by (<a href="#S2.E18" title="In Proof. ‣ 2 The 𝑛=3 case and its consequences ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>) leads to</p>
<table id="S2.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle M_{23}^{2}-M_{13}^{2}=\left(M_{23}^{2(p-1)/p}-M_{13}^{2(p-1)/p}\right)M_{12}^{2/p}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mn>23</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mn>13</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mn>23</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mn>13</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mn>12</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle M_{23}^{2}-M_{13}^{2}=\left(M_{23}^{2(p-1)/p}-M_{13}^{2(p-1)/p}\right)M_{12}^{2/p},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.I2.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">what in turn implies <math id="S2.I2.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{13}=M_{23}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>13</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>23</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{13}=M_{23}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="S2.I2.i1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">or</span> <math id="S2.I2.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{12}^{2/p}=\frac{M_{13}^{2}-M_{23}^{2}}{M_{13}^{2(p-1)/p}-M_{23}^{2(p-1)/p}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mn>12</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mn>13</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mn>23</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mn>13</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mn>23</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{12}^{2/p}=\frac{M_{13}^{2}-M_{23}^{2}}{M_{13}^{2(p-1)/p}-M_{23}^{2(p-1)/p}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.I2.i1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I2.i1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In the latter case, the triangle inequality (<a href="#S2.E12" title="In Proposition 7. ‣ 2 The 𝑛=3 case and its consequences ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>), in the current notation expressed simply as <math id="S2.I2.i1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{12}^{2/p}\leq M_{13}^{2/p}+M_{23}^{2/p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mn>12</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mn>13</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mn>23</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{12}^{2/p}\leq M_{13}^{2/p}+M_{23}^{2/p}</annotation></semantics></math>, is satisfied because</p>
<table id="S2.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle M_{12}^{2/p}=\frac{M_{13}^{2}-M_{23}^{2}}{M_{13}^{2(p-1)/p}-M_{23}^{2(p-1)/p}}\leq M_{13}^{2/p}+M_{23}^{2/p}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mn>12</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mn>13</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mn>23</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mn>13</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mn>23</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mn>13</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mn>23</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle M_{12}^{2/p}=\frac{M_{13}^{2}-M_{23}^{2}}{M_{13}^{2(p-1)/p}-M_{23}^{2(p-1)/p}}\leq M_{13}^{2/p}+M_{23}^{2/p},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.I2.i1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where the inequality follows<span id="footnote5" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">5</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">5</sup>
                    <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">5</span>
                    
                    
                    
                  To see how, divide both sides of the above inequality by <math id="footnote5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{13}^{2/p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mn>13</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{13}^{2/p}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="footnote5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{23}^{2/p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mn>23</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{23}^{2/p}</annotation></semantics></math>, depending on which is larger.</span></span></span> from <math id="S2.I2.i1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{a^{p}-1}{a^{p-1}-1}\leq a+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{a^{p}-1}{a^{p-1}-1}\leq a+1</annotation></semantics></math>, valid for any <math id="S2.I2.i1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.I2.i1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S2.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="S2.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textup{{x}}^{\dagger}\textup{{z}}\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textup{{x}}^{\dagger}\textup{{z}}\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S2.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha M_{12}^{2(p-1)/p}=-\gamma M_{23}^{2(p-1)/p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mn>12</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mn>23</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha M_{12}^{2(p-1)/p}=-\gamma M_{23}^{2(p-1)/p}</annotation></semantics></math>, which on the strength of (<a href="#S2.E18" title="In Proof. ‣ 2 The 𝑛=3 case and its consequences ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>) leads to <math id="S2.I2.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{13}^{2/p}=\frac{M_{12}^{2}-M_{23}^{2}}{M_{12}^{2(p-1)/p}+M_{23}^{2(p-1)/p}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mn>13</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mn>12</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mn>23</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mn>12</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mn>23</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{13}^{2/p}=\frac{M_{12}^{2}-M_{23}^{2}}{M_{12}^{2(p-1)/p}+M_{23}^{2(p-1)/p}}</annotation></semantics></math>. But the triangle inequality (<a href="#S2.E12" title="In Proposition 7. ‣ 2 The 𝑛=3 case and its consequences ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>) is then satisfied, because:</p>
<ul id="S2.I2.i2.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S2.I2.i2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="S2.I2.i2.I1.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="S2.I2.i2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I2.i2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="S2.I2.i2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{12}\geq M_{23}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>12</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>23</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{12}\geq M_{23}</annotation></semantics></math> one can estimate (using <math id="S2.I2.i2.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math> in the process)</p>
<table id="S2.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle M_{13}^{2/p}=\frac{M_{12}^{2}-M_{23}^{2}}{M_{12}^{2(p-1)/p}+M_{23}^{2(p-1)/p}}\geq M_{12}^{2/p}-M_{23}^{2/p}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mn>13</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mn>12</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mn>23</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mn>12</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mn>23</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mn>12</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mn>23</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle M_{13}^{2/p}=\frac{M_{12}^{2}-M_{23}^{2}}{M_{12}^{2(p-1)/p}+M_{23}^{2(p-1)/p}}\geq M_{12}^{2/p}-M_{23}^{2/p}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I2.i2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="S2.I2.i2.I1.i2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="S2.I2.i2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I2.i2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="S2.I2.i2.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{12}&lt;M_{23}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>12</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>23</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{12}&lt;M_{23}</annotation></semantics></math> one trivially has <math id="S2.I2.i2.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{12}^{2/p}\leq M_{13}^{2/p}+M_{23}^{2/p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mn>12</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mn>13</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mn>23</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{12}^{2/p}\leq M_{13}^{2/p}+M_{23}^{2/p}</annotation></semantics></math>, too.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S2.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="S2.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textup{{y}}^{\dagger}\textup{{z}}\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textup{{y}}^{\dagger}\textup{{z}}\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S2.I2.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta M_{12}^{2(p-1)/p}=-\gamma M_{13}^{2(p-1)/p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mn>12</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mn>13</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta M_{12}^{2(p-1)/p}=-\gamma M_{13}^{2(p-1)/p}</annotation></semantics></math>, which on the strength of (<a href="#S2.E18" title="In Proof. ‣ 2 The 𝑛=3 case and its consequences ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>) leads to <math id="S2.I2.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{23}^{2/p}=\frac{M_{12}^{2}-M_{13}^{2}}{M_{12}^{2(p-1)/p}+M_{13}^{2(p-1)/p}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mn>23</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mn>12</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mn>13</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mn>12</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mn>13</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{23}^{2/p}=\frac{M_{12}^{2}-M_{13}^{2}}{M_{12}^{2(p-1)/p}+M_{13}^{2(p-1)/p}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Similarly as in the previous case, the triangle inequality (<a href="#S2.E12" title="In Proposition 7. ‣ 2 The 𝑛=3 case and its consequences ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>) is then satisfied—simply swap <math id="S2.I2.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{23}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>23</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{23}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S2.I2.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{13}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>13</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{13}</annotation></semantics></math> in the above reasoning.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="S2.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">All in all, we are thus left with only two remaining cases:</span></p>
<ol id="S2.I3" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S2.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1<sup id="S2.I3.i1.1" class="ltx_sup">∘</sup></span> 
<div id="S2.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S2.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\textup{{x}},\textup{{y}},\textup{{z}}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\textup{{x}},\textup{{y}},\textup{{z}}\}</annotation></semantics></math> is an orthonormal system.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2<sup id="S2.I3.i2.1" class="ltx_sup">∘</sup></span> 
<div id="S2.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S2.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textup{{x}}^{\dagger}\textup{{z}}=\textup{{y}}^{\dagger}\textup{{z}}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textup{{x}}^{\dagger}\textup{{z}}=\textup{{y}}^{\dagger}\textup{{z}}=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.I3.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathbf{M}(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{z}})\|=\|\mathbf{M}(\textup{{y}}\times\textup{{z}})\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐌</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐌</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathbf{M}(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{z}})\|=\|\mathbf{M}(\textup{{y}}\times\textup{{z}})\|</annotation></semantics></math>, but <math id="S2.I3.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textup{{x}}^{\dagger}\textup{{y}}\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textup{{x}}^{\dagger}\textup{{y}}\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S2.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">The proof in case <math id="S2.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>1</mn><mo>∘</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math> is relatively straightforward. Introduce the orthonormal system <math id="S2.p14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{u}_{1}\vcentcolon=\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{u}_{1}\vcentcolon=\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{y}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.p14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{u}_{2}\vcentcolon=\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{z}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{u}_{2}\vcentcolon=\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{z}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.p14.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{u}_{3}\vcentcolon=\textup{{y}}\times\textup{{z}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{u}_{3}\vcentcolon=\textup{{y}}\times\textup{{z}}</annotation></semantics></math> and observe the following chain of (in)equalities:</span></p>
<table id="S2.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 2\|\textup{{E}}^{p/2}\mathbf{u}_{1}\|^{2/p}\leq 2\max_{\|\mathbf{v}\|=1}\|\textup{{E}}^{p/2}\mathbf{v}\|^{2/p}=2\rho(\textup{{E}})\leq\tr(\textup{{E}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">E</mtext><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐯</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">E</mtext><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐯</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">E</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">E</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 2\|\textup{{E}}^{p/2}\mathbf{u}_{1}\|^{2/p}\leq 2\max_{\|\mathbf{v}\|=1}\|\textup{{E}}^{p/2}\mathbf{v}\|^{2/p}=2\rho(\textup{{E}})\leq\tr(\textup{{E}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{3}\mathbf{u}_{i}^{\dagger}\textup{{E}}\mathbf{u}_{i}\leq\sum_{i=1}^{3}\left(\mathbf{u}_{i}^{\dagger}\textup{{E}}^{p/2}\mathbf{u}_{i}\right)^{2/p}\leq\sum_{i=1}^{3}\|\textup{{E}}^{p/2}\mathbf{u}_{i}\|^{2/p}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">E</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>†</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">E</mtext><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">E</mtext><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{3}\mathbf{u}_{i}^{\dagger}\textup{{E}}\mathbf{u}_{i}\leq\sum_{i=1}^{3}\left(\mathbf{u}_{i}^{\dagger}\textup{{E}}^{p/2}\mathbf{u}_{i}\right)^{2/p}\leq\sum_{i=1}^{3}\|\textup{{E}}^{p/2}\mathbf{u}_{i}\|^{2/p},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p14.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p14.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the second inequality is (<a href="#S2.E13" title="In Proposition 7. ‣ 2 The 𝑛=3 case and its consequences ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>), the third one follows from Jensen’s inequality (by the convexity of the map <math id="S2.p14.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\mapsto t^{p/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\mapsto t^{p/2}</annotation></semantics></math>), and the final one follows from the Cauchy–Schwarz inequality. Subtracting <math id="S2.p14.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\textup{{E}}^{p/2}\mathbf{u}_{1}\|^{2/p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">E</mtext><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐮</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\textup{{E}}^{p/2}\mathbf{u}_{1}\|^{2/p}</annotation></semantics></math> from both sides yields the triangle inequality (<a href="#S2.E12" title="In Proposition 7. ‣ 2 The 𝑛=3 case and its consequences ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text">In case <math id="S2.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>2</mn><mo>∘</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math>, notice first that a vector of unit length orthogonal to both <span id="S2.p15.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_bold">x</span> and <span id="S2.p15.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_bold">y</span> must be of the form</span></p>
<table id="S2.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.E19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\textup{{z}}=\textup{e}^{\textup{i}\phi}\frac{\bar{\textup{{x}}}\times\bar{\textup{{y}}}}{\|\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{y}}\|}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mtext>e</mtext><mrow><mtext>i</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mover accent="true"><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mover accent="true"><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\textup{{z}}=\textup{e}^{\textup{i}\phi}\frac{\bar{\textup{{x}}}\times\bar{\textup{{y}}}}{\|\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{y}}\|}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p15.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p15.2.1" class="ltx_text">Plugging this along with <math id="S2.p15.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{13}=M_{23}=\vcentcolon\Lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>13</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mn>23</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{13}=M_{23}=\vcentcolon\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math> into the third equation in (<a href="#S2.EGx14" title="Proof. ‣ 2 The 𝑛=3 case and its consequences ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>) yields</span></p>
<table id="S2.EGx22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bar{\textup{{x}}}\times\mathbf{M}^{2}((\bar{\textup{{x}}}\times\bar{\textup{{y}}})\times\textup{{x}})+\bar{\textup{{y}}}\times\mathbf{M}^{2}((\bar{\textup{{x}}}\times\bar{\textup{{y}}})\times\textup{{y}})=2\Lambda^{2}(\bar{\textup{{x}}}\times\bar{\textup{{y}}})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>𝐌</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mover accent="true"><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>𝐌</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mover accent="true"><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mover accent="true"><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bar{\textup{{x}}}\times\mathbf{M}^{2}((\bar{\textup{{x}}}\times\bar{\textup{{y}}})\times\textup{{x}})+\bar{\textup{{y}}}\times\mathbf{M}^{2}((\bar{\textup{{x}}}\times\bar{\textup{{y}}})\times\textup{{y}})=2\Lambda^{2}(\bar{\textup{{x}}}\times\bar{\textup{{y}}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p15.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p15.3.1" class="ltx_text">By (<a href="#S2.E7" title="In 2 The 𝑛=3 case and its consequences ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>), this simplifies to</span></p>
<table id="S2.EGx23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.E20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bar{\textup{{x}}}\times\mathbf{M}^{2}\bar{\textup{{y}}}-\bar{\textup{{y}}}\times\mathbf{M}^{2}\bar{\textup{{x}}}-(\textup{{y}}^{\dagger}\textup{{x}})\bar{\textup{{x}}}\times\mathbf{M}^{2}\bar{\textup{{x}}}+(\textup{{x}}^{\dagger}\textup{{y}})\bar{\textup{{y}}}\times\mathbf{M}^{2}\bar{\textup{{y}}}=2\Lambda^{2}(\bar{\textup{{x}}}\times\bar{\textup{{y}}})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>𝐌</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>𝐌</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>𝐌</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>𝐌</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mover accent="true"><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bar{\textup{{x}}}\times\mathbf{M}^{2}\bar{\textup{{y}}}-\bar{\textup{{y}}}\times\mathbf{M}^{2}\bar{\textup{{x}}}-(\textup{{y}}^{\dagger}\textup{{x}})\bar{\textup{{x}}}\times\mathbf{M}^{2}\bar{\textup{{x}}}+(\textup{{x}}^{\dagger}\textup{{y}})\bar{\textup{{y}}}\times\mathbf{M}^{2}\bar{\textup{{y}}}=2\Lambda^{2}(\bar{\textup{{x}}}\times\bar{\textup{{y}}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p15.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p15.4.1" class="ltx_text">Taking inner products with <span id="S2.p15.4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_bold">x</span>, <span id="S2.p15.4.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_bold">y</span> on both sides of (<a href="#S2.E20" title="In Proof. ‣ 2 The 𝑛=3 case and its consequences ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a>) yields, with the help of (<a href="#S2.E5" title="In 2 The 𝑛=3 case and its consequences ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>),</span></p>
<table id="S2.EGx24" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.EGx24.1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.EGx24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\{\begin{array}[]{l}-(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{y}})^{\dagger}\mathbf{M}^{2}\bar{\textup{{x}}}+(\textup{{x}}^{\dagger}\textup{{y}})(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{y}})^{\dagger}\mathbf{M}^{2}\bar{\textup{{y}}}=0\\[8.0pt]
-(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{y}})^{\dagger}\mathbf{M}^{2}\bar{\textup{{y}}}+(\textup{{y}}^{\dagger}\textup{{x}})(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{y}})^{\dagger}\mathbf{M}^{2}\bar{\textup{{x}}}=0\end{array}\right." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐌</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐌</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐌</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐌</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\{\begin{array}[]{l}-(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{y}})^{\dagger}\mathbf{M}^{2}\bar{\textup{{x}}}+(\textup{{x}}^{\dagger}\textup{{y}})(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{y}})^{\dagger}\mathbf{M}^{2}\bar{\textup{{y}}}=0\\[8.0pt]
-(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{y}})^{\dagger}\mathbf{M}^{2}\bar{\textup{{y}}}+(\textup{{y}}^{\dagger}\textup{{x}})(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{y}})^{\dagger}\mathbf{M}^{2}\bar{\textup{{x}}}=0\end{array}\right.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p15.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p15.5.1" class="ltx_text">what can be nicely expressed in the matrix form as</span></p>
<table id="S2.EGx25" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.EGx25.1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.EGx25.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left[\begin{array}[]{cc}-1&amp;\textup{{x}}^{\dagger}\textup{{y}}\\
\textup{{y}}^{\dagger}\textup{{x}}&amp;-1\end{array}\right]\left[\begin{array}[]{c}(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{y}})^{\dagger}\mathbf{M}^{2}\bar{\textup{{x}}}\\
(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{y}})^{\dagger}\mathbf{M}^{2}\bar{\textup{{y}}}\end{array}\right]=\left[\begin{array}[]{c}0\\
0\end{array}\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐌</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐌</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left[\begin{array}[]{cc}-1&amp;\textup{{x}}^{\dagger}\textup{{y}}\\
\textup{{y}}^{\dagger}\textup{{x}}&amp;-1\end{array}\right]\left[\begin{array}[]{c}(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{y}})^{\dagger}\mathbf{M}^{2}\bar{\textup{{x}}}\\
(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{y}})^{\dagger}\mathbf{M}^{2}\bar{\textup{{y}}}\end{array}\right]=\left[\begin{array}[]{c}0\\
0\end{array}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p15.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p15.6.1" class="ltx_text">But since <math id="S2.p15.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-|\textup{{x}}^{\dagger}\textup{{y}}|^{2}=\|\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{y}}\|^{2}\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-|\textup{{x}}^{\dagger}\textup{{y}}|^{2}=\|\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{y}}\|^{2}\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math> by assumption, equation (<a href="#S2.EGx25" title="Proof. ‣ 2 The 𝑛=3 case and its consequences ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>) yields <math id="S2.p15.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{y}})^{\dagger}\mathbf{M}^{2}\bar{\textup{{x}}}=(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{y}})^{\dagger}\mathbf{M}^{2}\bar{\textup{{y}}}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐌</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐌</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{y}})^{\dagger}\mathbf{M}^{2}\bar{\textup{{x}}}=(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{y}})^{\dagger}\mathbf{M}^{2}\bar{\textup{{y}}}=0</annotation></semantics></math>. In other words, the vector <math id="S2.p15.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{M}^{2}(\bar{\textup{{x}}}\times\bar{\textup{{y}}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐌</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mover accent="true"><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{M}^{2}(\bar{\textup{{x}}}\times\bar{\textup{{y}}})</annotation></semantics></math> is orthogonal to both <span id="S2.p15.6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_bold">x</span> and <span id="S2.p15.6.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_bold">y</span>, and hence must be proportional to <math id="S2.p15.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\textup{{x}}}\times\bar{\textup{{y}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mover accent="true"><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\textup{{x}}}\times\bar{\textup{{y}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., it must be an <em id="S2.p15.6.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">eigenvector</em> of <math id="S2.p15.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{M}^{2}=\textup{{E}}^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐌</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">E</mtext><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{M}^{2}=\textup{{E}}^{p}</annotation></semantics></math>, corresponding to, say, the eigenvalue <math id="S2.p15.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{3}^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mn>3</mn><mi>p</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{3}^{p}</annotation></semantics></math> (without loss of generality).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p16" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p16.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p16.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S2.p16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{v}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.p16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{v}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> be the other two eigenvectors of <math id="S2.p16.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textup{{E}}^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">E</mtext><mi>p</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textup{{E}}^{p}</annotation></semantics></math> with eigenvalues <math id="S2.p16.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{1}^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>p</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{1}^{p}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.p16.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{2}^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>p</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{2}^{p}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively. Bearing in mind (<a href="#S2.E19" title="In Proof. ‣ 2 The 𝑛=3 case and its consequences ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>), the vectors <math id="S2.p16.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{z}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{z}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.p16.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textup{{y}}\times\textup{{z}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textup{{y}}\times\textup{{z}}</annotation></semantics></math> both lie in <math id="S2.p16.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textnormal{span}\{\mathbf{v}_{1},\mathbf{v}_{2}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>span</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textnormal{span}\{\mathbf{v}_{1},\mathbf{v}_{2}\}</annotation></semantics></math> and their norm is 1 (recall we have <math id="S2.p16.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textup{{x}}^{\dagger}\textup{{z}}=\textup{{y}}^{\dagger}\textup{{z}}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textup{{x}}^{\dagger}\textup{{z}}=\textup{{y}}^{\dagger}\textup{{z}}=0</annotation></semantics></math> in the considered case), and so we can decompose them as</span></p>
<table id="S2.EGx26" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.E27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E27.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{z}}=\mathbf{v}_{1}\textup{e}^{\textup{i}\xi_{1}}\cos\varphi+\mathbf{v}_{2}\textup{e}^{\textup{i}\xi_{2}}\sin\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mtext>e</mtext><mrow><mtext>i</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mtext>e</mtext><mrow><mtext>i</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{z}}=\mathbf{v}_{1}\textup{e}^{\textup{i}\xi_{1}}\cos\varphi+\mathbf{v}_{2}\textup{e}^{\textup{i}\xi_{2}}\sin\varphi</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.Ex25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\textup{{y}}\times\textup{{z}}=\mathbf{v}_{1}\textup{e}^{\textup{i}\eta_{1}}\cos\theta+\mathbf{v}_{2}\textup{e}^{\textup{i}\eta_{2}}\sin\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mtext>e</mtext><mrow><mtext>i</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mtext>e</mtext><mrow><mtext>i</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\textup{{y}}\times\textup{{z}}=\mathbf{v}_{1}\textup{e}^{\textup{i}\eta_{1}}\cos\theta+\mathbf{v}_{2}\textup{e}^{\textup{i}\eta_{2}}\sin\theta</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p16.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p16.2.1" class="ltx_text">for some angles <math id="S2.p16.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi_{1},\xi_{2},\varphi,\eta_{1},\eta_{2},\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi_{1},\xi_{2},\varphi,\eta_{1},\eta_{2},\theta</annotation></semantics></math>. With all that in mind, our desired triangle inequality (<a href="#S2.E12" title="In Proposition 7. ‣ 2 The 𝑛=3 case and its consequences ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>) reduces to</span></p>
<table id="S2.EGx27" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.Ex26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lambda_{3}\|\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{y}}\|^{2/p}\leq\left(\lambda_{1}^{p}\cos^{2}\varphi+\lambda_{2}^{p}\sin^{2}\varphi\right)^{1/p}+\left(\lambda_{1}^{p}\cos^{2}\theta+\lambda_{2}^{p}\sin^{2}\theta\right)^{1/p}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>p</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msup><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>p</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msup><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>p</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msup><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>p</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msup><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lambda_{3}\|\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{y}}\|^{2/p}\leq\left(\lambda_{1}^{p}\cos^{2}\varphi+\lambda_{2}^{p}\sin^{2}\varphi\right)^{1/p}+\left(\lambda_{1}^{p}\cos^{2}\theta+\lambda_{2}^{p}\sin^{2}\theta\right)^{1/p}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p16.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p16.3.1" class="ltx_text">The troublesome <math id="S2.p16.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{y}}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{y}}\|</annotation></semantics></math> lingering on the left-hand side can be expressed in the language of the above angles, too. Indeed, by (<a href="#S2.E19" title="In Proof. ‣ 2 The 𝑛=3 case and its consequences ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>) and (<a href="#S2.E8" title="In 2 The 𝑛=3 case and its consequences ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>) we have that</span></p>
<table id="S2.EGx28" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.Ex27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{z}})\times(\textup{{y}}\times\textup{{z}})=\textup{e}^{2\textup{i}\phi}\,\bar{\textup{{x}}}\times\bar{\textup{{y}}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mtext>e</mtext><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>i</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mover accent="true"><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{z}})\times(\textup{{y}}\times\textup{{z}})=\textup{e}^{2\textup{i}\phi}\,\bar{\textup{{x}}}\times\bar{\textup{{y}}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p16.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p16.4.1" class="ltx_text">and so, introducing an auxilliary angle <math id="S2.p16.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega\vcentcolon=\tfrac{1}{2}(\xi_{2}-\xi_{1}+\eta_{1}-\eta_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega\vcentcolon=\tfrac{1}{2}(\xi_{2}-\xi_{1}+\eta_{1}-\eta_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>, after some trigonometry we obtain</span></p>
<table id="S2.EGx29" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.Ex28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{y}}\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{y}}\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex28.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\|(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{z}})\times(\textup{{y}}\times\textup{{z}})\|^{2}=|\cos\varphi\sin\theta-\textup{e}^{2\textup{i}\omega}\sin\varphi\cos\theta|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mtext>e</mtext><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>i</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\|(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{z}})\times(\textup{{y}}\times\textup{{z}})\|^{2}=|\cos\varphi\sin\theta-\textup{e}^{2\textup{i}\omega}\sin\varphi\cos\theta|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.Ex29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\cos^{2}\omega\sin^{2}(\theta-\varphi)+\sin^{2}\omega\sin^{2}(\theta+\varphi)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msup><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msup><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\cos^{2}\omega\sin^{2}(\theta-\varphi)+\sin^{2}\omega\sin^{2}(\theta+\varphi).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p16.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p16.5.1" class="ltx_text">Notice that the right-hand side can be estimated from above by <math id="S2.p16.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max\{\sin^{2}(\theta\pm\varphi)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msup><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>±</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max\{\sin^{2}(\theta\pm\varphi)\}</annotation></semantics></math>, so in order to prove the triangle inequality (<a href="#S2.E12" title="In Proposition 7. ‣ 2 The 𝑛=3 case and its consequences ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>) it suffices to show that</span></p>
<table id="S2.EGx30" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.E28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(\lambda_{1}+\lambda_{2})|\sin(\theta\pm\varphi)|^{2/p}\leq\left(\lambda_{1}^{p}\cos^{2}\varphi+\lambda_{2}^{p}\sin^{2}\varphi\right)^{1/p}+\left(\lambda_{1}^{p}\cos^{2}\theta+\lambda_{2}^{p}\sin^{2}\theta\right)^{1/p}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>±</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>p</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msup><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>p</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msup><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>p</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msup><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>p</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msup><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(\lambda_{1}+\lambda_{2})|\sin(\theta\pm\varphi)|^{2/p}\leq\left(\lambda_{1}^{p}\cos^{2}\varphi+\lambda_{2}^{p}\sin^{2}\varphi\right)^{1/p}+\left(\lambda_{1}^{p}\cos^{2}\theta+\lambda_{2}^{p}\sin^{2}\theta\right)^{1/p},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p16.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p16.6.1" class="ltx_text">where we have also replaced <math id="S2.p16.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{3}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S2.p16.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{1}+\lambda_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{1}+\lambda_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, which by (<a href="#S2.E13" title="In Proposition 7. ‣ 2 The 𝑛=3 case and its consequences ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>) is the former’s upper bound.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p17" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p17.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p17.1.1" class="ltx_text">Luckily, we do not have to attack (<a href="#S2.E28" title="In Proof. ‣ 2 The 𝑛=3 case and its consequences ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">28</span></a>) in full generality, as we still have not taken full advantage of the assumption <math id="S2.p17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathbf{M}(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{z}})\|=\|\mathbf{M}(\textup{{y}}\times\textup{{z}})\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐌</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐌</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathbf{M}(\textup{{x}}\times\textup{{z}})\|=\|\mathbf{M}(\textup{{y}}\times\textup{{z}})\|</annotation></semantics></math>. Indeed, when we substitute (<a href="#S2.E27" title="In Proof. ‣ 2 The 𝑛=3 case and its consequences ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">27</span></a>) and <math id="S2.p17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{M}=\textup{{E}}^{p/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐌</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">E</mtext><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{M}=\textup{{E}}^{p/2}</annotation></semantics></math> into this assumption, after some trigonometry it reduces to</span></p>
<table id="S2.EGx31" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.E29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(\lambda_{2}^{p}-\lambda_{1}^{p})\sin(\theta-\varphi)\sin(\theta+\varphi)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>p</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>p</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(\lambda_{2}^{p}-\lambda_{1}^{p})\sin(\theta-\varphi)\sin(\theta+\varphi)=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p17.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p17.2.1" class="ltx_text">and we are thus left with three possibilities.</span></p>
<ul id="S2.I4" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S2.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S2.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="S2.I4.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{1}=\lambda_{2}=\vcentcolon\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{1}=\lambda_{2}=\vcentcolon\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>, then the LHS of (<a href="#S2.E28" title="In Proof. ‣ 2 The 𝑛=3 case and its consequences ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">28</span></a>) becomes <math id="S2.I4.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\lambda|\sin(\theta\pm\varphi)|^{2/p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>±</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\lambda|\sin(\theta\pm\varphi)|^{2/p}</annotation></semantics></math>, whereas the RHS reduces to <math id="S2.I4.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>, and so the inequality clearly holds.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S2.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="S2.I4.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sin(\theta-\varphi)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sin(\theta-\varphi)=0</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S2.I4.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi=\theta+k\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi=\theta+k\pi</annotation></semantics></math> and (<a href="#S2.E28" title="In Proof. ‣ 2 The 𝑛=3 case and its consequences ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">28</span></a>) boils down to showing that</p>
<table id="S2.EGx32" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.E30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(\lambda_{1}+\lambda_{2})^{p}\sin^{2}2\theta\leq 2^{p}\left(\lambda_{1}^{p}\cos^{2}\theta+\lambda_{2}^{p}\sin^{2}\theta\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msup><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>p</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>p</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msup><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>p</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msup><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(\lambda_{1}+\lambda_{2})^{p}\sin^{2}2\theta\leq 2^{p}\left(\lambda_{1}^{p}\cos^{2}\theta+\lambda_{2}^{p}\sin^{2}\theta\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.I4.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Indeed, by the convexity of the map <math id="S2.I4.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\mapsto t^{p/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\mapsto t^{p/2}</annotation></semantics></math>, one can write that</p>
<table id="S2.EGx33" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.Ex30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left(\tfrac{\lambda_{1}+\lambda_{2}}{2}\right)^{p}\sin^{2}2\theta\leq\Big(\tfrac{\lambda_{1}^{p/2}}{2}+\tfrac{\lambda_{2}^{p/2}}{2}\Big)^{2}\sin^{2}2\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msup><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msup><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left(\tfrac{\lambda_{1}+\lambda_{2}}{2}\right)^{p}\sin^{2}2\theta\leq\Big(\tfrac{\lambda_{1}^{p/2}}{2}+\tfrac{\lambda_{2}^{p/2}}{2}\Big)^{2}\sin^{2}2\theta</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.Ex31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\big(\lambda_{1}^{p}\cos^{2}\theta+\lambda_{2}^{p}\sin^{2}\theta\big)-\big(\lambda_{1}^{p/2}\cos^{2}\theta-\lambda_{2}^{p/2}\sin^{2}\theta\big)^{2}\leq\big(\lambda_{1}^{p}\cos^{2}\theta+\lambda_{2}^{p}\sin^{2}\theta\big)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>p</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msup><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>p</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msup><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msup><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msup><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>p</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msup><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>p</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msup><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\big(\lambda_{1}^{p}\cos^{2}\theta+\lambda_{2}^{p}\sin^{2}\theta\big)-\big(\lambda_{1}^{p/2}\cos^{2}\theta-\lambda_{2}^{p/2}\sin^{2}\theta\big)^{2}\leq\big(\lambda_{1}^{p}\cos^{2}\theta+\lambda_{2}^{p}\sin^{2}\theta\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I4.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S2.I4.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I4.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="S2.I4.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sin(\theta+\varphi)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>φ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sin(\theta+\varphi)=0</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S2.I4.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi=-\theta+k\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi=-\theta+k\pi</annotation></semantics></math> and (<a href="#S2.E28" title="In Proof. ‣ 2 The 𝑛=3 case and its consequences ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">28</span></a>) again boils down to (<a href="#S2.E30" title="In 2nd item ‣ Proof. ‣ 2 The 𝑛=3 case and its consequences ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">30</span></a>).</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="S2.p17.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p17.3.1" class="ltx_text">This finishes the analysis of case <math id="S2.p17.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>2</mn><mo>∘</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math> and concludes the whole proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.p18" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p18.1" class="ltx_p">Let now <math id="S2.p18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 3</annotation></semantics></math> and recall that <math id="S2.p18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{p}(\textup{{x}},\textup{{y}})\vcentcolon=\|\textup{{E}}^{p/2}(\textup{{x}}\wedge\textup{{y}})\|^{2/p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">E</mtext><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo>∧</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{p}(\textup{{x}},\textup{{y}})\vcentcolon=\|\textup{{E}}^{p/2}(\textup{{x}}\wedge\textup{{y}})\|^{2/p}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S2.p18.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textup{{E}}\in\mathcal{B}(\Lambda^{2}{\mathbb{C}}^{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">E</mtext><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textup{{E}}\in\mathcal{B}(\Lambda^{2}{\mathbb{C}}^{n})</annotation></semantics></math> is a positive-definite operator defined via <math id="S2.p18.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textup{{E}}(\mathbf{e}_{i}\wedge\mathbf{e}_{j})\vcentcolon=E_{ij}\mathbf{e}_{i}\wedge\mathbf{e}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">E</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∧</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>∧</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textup{{E}}(\mathbf{e}_{i}\wedge\mathbf{e}_{j})\vcentcolon=E_{ij}\mathbf{e}_{i}\wedge\mathbf{e}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="S2.p18.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i,j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i,j</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S2.p18.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(E_{ij})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(E_{ij})</annotation></semantics></math> is some fixed distance matrix. The following partial result demonstrates that in order to establish the triangle inequality (<a href="#S1.E4" title="In Theorem 2. ‣ 1 Introduction and main result ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>), it suffices to focus on <em id="S2.p18.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">orthonormal</em> systems of vectors.</p>
</div>
<div id="ThmThm8" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_Prop">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="ThmThm8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 8</span></span><span id="ThmThm8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="ThmThm8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="ThmThm8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="ThmThm8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Triangle inequality (<a href="#S1.E4" title="In Theorem 2. ‣ 1 Introduction and main result ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>) holds if and only if</span></p>
<table id="S2.EGx34" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.E31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\textup{{E}}^{p/2}(\mathbf{u}\wedge\mathbf{v})\|^{2/p}\leq\|\textup{{E}}^{p/2}(\mathbf{u}\wedge\mathbf{w})\|^{2/p}+\|\textup{{E}}^{p/2}(\mathbf{v}\wedge\mathbf{w})\|^{2/p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">E</mtext><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐮</mi><mo>∧</mo><mi>𝐯</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">E</mtext><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐮</mi><mo>∧</mo><mi>𝐰</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">E</mtext><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>∧</mo><mi>𝐰</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\textup{{E}}^{p/2}(\mathbf{u}\wedge\mathbf{v})\|^{2/p}\leq\|\textup{{E}}^{p/2}(\mathbf{u}\wedge\mathbf{w})\|^{2/p}+\|\textup{{E}}^{p/2}(\mathbf{v}\wedge\mathbf{w})\|^{2/p}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="ThmThm8.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="ThmThm8.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">for any <em id="ThmThm8.p1.2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">orthonormal</em> <math id="ThmThm8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathbf{u},\mathbf{v},\mathbf{w}\}\subset{\mathbb{C}}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>𝐮</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐰</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathbf{u},\mathbf{v},\mathbf{w}\}\subset{\mathbb{C}}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S2.p19" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p19.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p19.1.1" class="ltx_text">Assume (<a href="#S2.E31" title="In Proposition 8. ‣ 2 The 𝑛=3 case and its consequences ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">31</span></a>) holds. Fix norm-one vectors <math id="S2.p19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textup{{x}},\textup{{y}},\textup{{z}}\in{\mathbb{C}}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo>,</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textup{{x}},\textup{{y}},\textup{{z}}\in{\mathbb{C}}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> and define <math id="S2.p19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math> to be any 3-dimensional subspace containing them<span id="footnote6" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">6</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">6</sup>
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">6</span>
                
                
                
              If the system <math id="footnote6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\textup{{x}},\textup{{y}},\textup{{z}}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\textup{{x}},\textup{{y}},\textup{{z}}\}</annotation></semantics></math> is linearly independent, then of course <math id="footnote6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math> is simply its span.</span></span></span> along with <math id="S2.p19.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda^{2}V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda^{2}V</annotation></semantics></math> being the corresponding 3-dimensional subspace of <math id="S2.p19.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda^{2}{\mathbb{C}}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda^{2}{\mathbb{C}}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="S2.p19.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h:\Lambda^{2}V\times\Lambda^{2}V\rightarrow{\mathbb{R}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h:\Lambda^{2}V\times\Lambda^{2}V\rightarrow{\mathbb{R}}</annotation></semantics></math> be the restriction of the Hermitian form <math id="S2.p19.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda^{2}{\mathbb{C}}^{n}\times\Lambda^{2}{\mathbb{C}}^{n}\ni(\mathbf{V},\mathbf{W})\mapsto\langle\mathbf{V}|\textup{{E}}^{p}\mathbf{W}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><mo>∋</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐖</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>𝐕</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">E</mtext><mi>p</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐖</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda^{2}{\mathbb{C}}^{n}\times\Lambda^{2}{\mathbb{C}}^{n}\ni(\mathbf{V},\mathbf{W})\mapsto\langle\mathbf{V}|\textup{{E}}^{p}\mathbf{W}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="S2.p19.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathbf{B}_{1},\mathbf{B}_{2},\mathbf{B}_{3}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝐁</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐁</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐁</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathbf{B}_{1},\mathbf{B}_{2},\mathbf{B}_{3}\}</annotation></semantics></math> be its orthonormal eigenbasis, i.e. a basis of <math id="S2.p19.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda^{2}V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda^{2}V</annotation></semantics></math> in which the matrix of <math id="S2.p19.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>, denoted by <math id="S2.p19.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐇</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{H}</annotation></semantics></math>, is diagonal, <math id="S2.p19.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{H}=\diag(\mu_{1},\mu_{2},\mu_{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐇</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{H}=\diag(\mu_{1},\mu_{2},\mu_{3})</annotation></semantics></math>. We claim that <math id="S2.p19.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\rho(\mathbf{H}^{2/p})\leq\tr\mathbf{H}^{2/p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\rho(\mathbf{H}^{2/p})\leq\tr\mathbf{H}^{2/p}</annotation></semantics></math>, what on the strength of Proposition <a href="#ThmThm7" title="Proposition 7. ‣ 2 The 𝑛=3 case and its consequences ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> would finish the proof.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p20" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p20.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p20.1.1" class="ltx_text">In order to prove the claim we shall first find an orthonormal basis <math id="S2.p20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathbf{f}_{1},\mathbf{f}_{2},\mathbf{f}_{3}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝐟</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐟</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐟</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathbf{f}_{1},\mathbf{f}_{2},\mathbf{f}_{3}\}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="S2.EGx35" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.E32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{B}_{1}=\mathbf{f}_{2}\wedge\mathbf{f}_{3},\qquad\mathbf{B}_{2}=\mathbf{f}_{3}\wedge\mathbf{f}_{1},\qquad\mathbf{B}_{3}=\mathbf{f}_{1}\wedge\mathbf{f}_{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐁</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐟</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∧</mo><msub><mi>𝐟</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐁</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐟</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>∧</mo><msub><mi>𝐟</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐁</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐟</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∧</mo><msub><mi>𝐟</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{B}_{1}=\mathbf{f}_{2}\wedge\mathbf{f}_{3},\qquad\mathbf{B}_{2}=\mathbf{f}_{3}\wedge\mathbf{f}_{1},\qquad\mathbf{B}_{3}=\mathbf{f}_{1}\wedge\mathbf{f}_{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p20.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p20.2.1" class="ltx_text">what is possible due to the three-dimensionality of <math id="S2.p20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math> with the help of the complex Hodge star operator<span id="footnote7" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">7</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">7</sup>
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">7</span>
                
                
                
              For an alternative, matrix-theoretical justification see <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>, Lemma 3.1]</cite>.</span></span></span> (cf. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">20</a>]</cite>). Concretely, let <math id="S2.p20.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathbf{v}_{1},\mathbf{v}_{2},\mathbf{v}_{3}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathbf{v}_{1},\mathbf{v}_{2},\mathbf{v}_{3}\}</annotation></semantics></math> be an orthonormal basis of <math id="S2.p20.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math> such that the matrix <math id="S2.p20.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(U_{ij})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(U_{ij})</annotation></semantics></math> changing the basis from <math id="S2.p20.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathbf{B}_{1},\mathbf{B}_{2},\mathbf{B}_{3}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝐁</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐁</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐁</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathbf{B}_{1},\mathbf{B}_{2},\mathbf{B}_{3}\}</annotation></semantics></math> to the ‘new’ basis <math id="S2.p20.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathbf{v}_{2}\wedge\mathbf{v}_{3},\mathbf{v}_{3}\wedge\mathbf{v}_{1},\mathbf{v}_{1}\wedge\mathbf{v}_{2}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∧</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>∧</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∧</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathbf{v}_{2}\wedge\mathbf{v}_{3},\mathbf{v}_{3}\wedge\mathbf{v}_{1},\mathbf{v}_{1}\wedge\mathbf{v}_{2}\}</annotation></semantics></math> has determinant 1 (which can always be ensured by adjusting the phase factors). Define the operator <math id="S2.p20.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\star:V\rightarrow\Lambda^{2}V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">⋆</mo><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\star:V\rightarrow\Lambda^{2}V</annotation></semantics></math> by (linearly extending) the formulas</span></p>
<table id="S2.EGx36" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.Ex32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\star\mathbf{v}_{1}\vcentcolon=\bar{\mathbf{v}}_{2}\wedge\bar{\mathbf{v}}_{3},\qquad\star\mathbf{v}_{2}\vcentcolon=\bar{\mathbf{v}}_{3}\wedge\bar{\mathbf{v}}_{1},\qquad\star\mathbf{v}_{3}\vcentcolon=\bar{\mathbf{v}}_{1}\wedge\bar{\mathbf{v}}_{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋆</mo><mi>𝐯</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∧</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>3</mn></msub><mo rspace="1.833em">,</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">⋆</mo><mi>𝐯</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>∧</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="1.833em">,</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">⋆</mo><mi>𝐯</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∧</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\star\mathbf{v}_{1}\vcentcolon=\bar{\mathbf{v}}_{2}\wedge\bar{\mathbf{v}}_{3},\qquad\star\mathbf{v}_{2}\vcentcolon=\bar{\mathbf{v}}_{3}\wedge\bar{\mathbf{v}}_{1},\qquad\star\mathbf{v}_{3}\vcentcolon=\bar{\mathbf{v}}_{1}\wedge\bar{\mathbf{v}}_{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p20.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p20.3.1" class="ltx_text">Clearly, <math id="S2.p20.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\star" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⋆</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\star</annotation></semantics></math> is unitary, satisfies</span></p>
<table id="S2.EGx37" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.E33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\langle\overline{\star\mathbf{v}_{i}}|\mathbf{v}_{j}\wedge\mathbf{v}_{k}\rangle=\varepsilon_{ijk},\qquad i,j,k=1,2,3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mover accent="true"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋆</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∧</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\langle\overline{\star\mathbf{v}_{i}}|\mathbf{v}_{j}\wedge\mathbf{v}_{k}\rangle=\varepsilon_{ijk},\qquad i,j,k=1,2,3</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(33)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p20.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p20.4.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="S2.p20.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{ijk}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{ijk}</annotation></semantics></math> is the Levi-Civita symbol, and allows us to express the new basis as <math id="S2.p20.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\overline{\star\mathbf{v}_{1}},\overline{\star\mathbf{v}_{2}},\overline{\star\mathbf{v}_{3}}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mover accent="true"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋆</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋆</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋆</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\overline{\star\mathbf{v}_{1}},\overline{\star\mathbf{v}_{2}},\overline{\star\mathbf{v}_{3}}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, along with the entries of the change-of-basis matrix as <math id="S2.p20.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{ij}=\langle\overline{\star\mathbf{v}_{j}}|\mathbf{B}_{i}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mover accent="true"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋆</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐁</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{ij}=\langle\overline{\star\mathbf{v}_{j}}|\mathbf{B}_{i}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p21" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p21.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p21.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now, set <math id="S2.p21.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{f}_{l}\vcentcolon=\star^{-1}\bar{\mathbf{B}}_{l}=\sum_{m}\bar{U}_{lm}\mathbf{v}_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐟</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">:=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋆</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐁</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mo>∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mi>𝐯</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{f}_{l}\vcentcolon=\star^{-1}\bar{\mathbf{B}}_{l}=\sum_{m}\bar{U}_{lm}\mathbf{v}_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.p21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l=1,2,3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l=1,2,3</annotation></semantics></math>. By the unitarity of <math id="S2.p21.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\star" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⋆</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\star</annotation></semantics></math>, thus defined system <math id="S2.p21.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathbf{f}_{1},\mathbf{f}_{2},\mathbf{f}_{3}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝐟</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐟</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐟</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathbf{f}_{1},\mathbf{f}_{2},\mathbf{f}_{3}\}</annotation></semantics></math> is orthonormal. To see that it satisfies (<a href="#S2.E32" title="In Proof. ‣ 2 The 𝑛=3 case and its consequences ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">32</span></a>), take, e.g., <math id="S2.p21.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{f}_{2}\wedge\mathbf{f}_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐟</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∧</mo><msub><mi>𝐟</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{f}_{2}\wedge\mathbf{f}_{3}</annotation></semantics></math> and calculate its inner products with <math id="S2.p21.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{B}_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐁</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{B}_{l}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.p21.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l=1,2,3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l=1,2,3</annotation></semantics></math>, obtaining</span></p>
<table id="S2.EGx38" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.Ex33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\langle\mathbf{B}_{l}|\mathbf{f}_{2}\wedge\mathbf{f}_{3}\rangle=\langle\sumka_{i}U_{li}\overline{\star\mathbf{v}_{i}}|(\sumka_{j}\bar{U}_{2j}\mathbf{v}_{j})\wedge(\sumka_{k}\bar{U}_{3k}\mathbf{v}_{k})\rangle=\sumka_{ijk}\bar{U}_{li}\bar{U}_{2j}\bar{U}_{3k}\varepsilon_{ijk}=\begin{cases}1&amp;\textnormal{for }l=1\\
0&amp;\textnormal{otherwise}\end{cases}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>𝐁</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐟</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∧</mo><msub><mi>𝐟</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">∑</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>li</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋆</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">∑</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">∑</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">∑</mi><mi>ijk</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>li</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>U</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>ijk</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>for </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mtext>otherwise</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\langle\mathbf{B}_{l}|\mathbf{f}_{2}\wedge\mathbf{f}_{3}\rangle=\langle\sumka_{i}U_{li}\overline{\star\mathbf{v}_{i}}|(\sumka_{j}\bar{U}_{2j}\mathbf{v}_{j})\wedge(\sumka_{k}\bar{U}_{3k}\mathbf{v}_{k})\rangle=\sumka_{ijk}\bar{U}_{li}\bar{U}_{2j}\bar{U}_{3k}\varepsilon_{ijk}=\begin{cases}1&amp;\textnormal{for }l=1\\
0&amp;\textnormal{otherwise}\end{cases},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p21.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p21.2.1" class="ltx_text">where we have expanded <math id="S2.p21.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{B}_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐁</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{B}_{l}</annotation></semantics></math> in the basis <math id="S2.p21.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\overline{\star\mathbf{v}_{i}}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mover accent="true"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋆</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\overline{\star\mathbf{v}_{i}}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, used (<a href="#S2.E33" title="In Proof. ‣ 2 The 𝑛=3 case and its consequences ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">33</span></a>) and recognized the formula for the (complex conjugate of the) determinant of a <math id="S2.p21.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3\times 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3\times 3</annotation></semantics></math> matrix. This proves that indeed <math id="S2.p21.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{f}_{2}\wedge\mathbf{f}_{3}=\mathbf{B}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐟</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∧</mo><msub><mi>𝐟</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝐁</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{f}_{2}\wedge\mathbf{f}_{3}=\mathbf{B}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and the other two equalities in (<a href="#S2.E32" title="In Proof. ‣ 2 The 𝑛=3 case and its consequences ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">32</span></a>) can be shown similarly.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p22" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p22.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p22.1.1" class="ltx_text">Having established (<a href="#S2.E32" title="In Proof. ‣ 2 The 𝑛=3 case and its consequences ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">32</span></a>), we can now write</span></p>
<table id="S2.EGx39" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.Ex34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mu_{1}=\sqrt{h(\mathbf{B}_{1},\mathbf{B}_{1})}=\|\textup{{E}}^{p/2}(\mathbf{f}_{2}\wedge\mathbf{f}_{3})\|," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐁</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐁</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">E</mtext><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐟</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∧</mo><msub><mi>𝐟</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mu_{1}=\sqrt{h(\mathbf{B}_{1},\mathbf{B}_{1})}=\|\textup{{E}}^{p/2}(\mathbf{f}_{2}\wedge\mathbf{f}_{3})\|,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.Ex35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mu_{2}=\sqrt{h(\mathbf{B}_{2},\mathbf{B}_{2})}=\|\textup{{E}}^{p/2}(\mathbf{f}_{1}\wedge\mathbf{f}_{3})\|," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐁</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐁</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">E</mtext><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐟</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∧</mo><msub><mi>𝐟</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mu_{2}=\sqrt{h(\mathbf{B}_{2},\mathbf{B}_{2})}=\|\textup{{E}}^{p/2}(\mathbf{f}_{1}\wedge\mathbf{f}_{3})\|,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.Ex36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mu_{3}=\sqrt{h(\mathbf{B}_{3},\mathbf{B}_{3})}=\|\textup{{E}}^{p/2}(\mathbf{f}_{1}\wedge\mathbf{f}_{2})\|," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐁</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐁</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">E</mtext><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐟</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∧</mo><msub><mi>𝐟</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mu_{3}=\sqrt{h(\mathbf{B}_{3},\mathbf{B}_{3})}=\|\textup{{E}}^{p/2}(\mathbf{f}_{1}\wedge\mathbf{f}_{2})\|,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p22.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p22.2.1" class="ltx_text">and our assumption (<a href="#S2.E31" title="In Proposition 8. ‣ 2 The 𝑛=3 case and its consequences ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">31</span></a>) immediately yields <math id="S2.p22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\max_{i}\mu_{i}^{2/p}\leq\sum_{j}\mu_{j}^{2/p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\max_{i}\mu_{i}^{2/p}\leq\sum_{j}\mu_{j}^{2/p}</annotation></semantics></math>, what is exactly our desired condition <math id="S2.p22.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\rho(\mathbf{H}^{2/p})\leq\tr\mathbf{H}^{2/p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\rho(\mathbf{H}^{2/p})\leq\tr\mathbf{H}^{2/p}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">3 </span>A certain convexity result and the proof of the triangle inequality</h2>

<div id="S3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The proof of Theorem <a href="#ThmThm2" title="Theorem 2. ‣ 1 Introduction and main result ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> will be a consequence of the following convexity result involving the squared moduli of certain minors of order 2 and 3.</p>
</div>
<div id="ThmThm9" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_Thm">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="ThmThm9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 9</span></span><span id="ThmThm9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="ThmThm9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="ThmThm9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="ThmThm9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix <math id="ThmThm9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 3</annotation></semantics></math>. For any symmetric matrix <math id="ThmThm9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a_{ij})\in\mathbb{M}_{n}({\mathbb{R}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝕄</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ℝ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a_{ij})\in\mathbb{M}_{n}({\mathbb{R}})</annotation></semantics></math> with nonnegative entries, any orthonormal system <math id="ThmThm9.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\textup{{x}},\textup{{y}},\textup{{z}}\}\subset{\mathbb{C}}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\textup{{x}},\textup{{y}},\textup{{z}}\}\subset{\mathbb{C}}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> and any jointly convex, completely symmetric map <math id="ThmThm9.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}^{3}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}^{3}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx40" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f\Big(\sum_{i&lt;j}a_{ij}\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}x_{i}&amp;x_{j}\\
y_{i}&amp;y_{j}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2},\sum_{i&lt;k}a_{ik}\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}x_{i}&amp;x_{k}\\
z_{i}&amp;z_{k}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2},\sum_{j&lt;k}a_{jk}\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}y_{j}&amp;y_{k}\\
z_{j}&amp;z_{k}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2}\Big)\leq\sum_{i&lt;j&lt;k}f(a_{ij},a_{ik},a_{jk})\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}x_{i}&amp;x_{j}&amp;x_{k}\\
y_{i}&amp;y_{j}&amp;y_{k}\\
z_{i}&amp;z_{j}&amp;z_{k}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f\Big(\sum_{i&lt;j}a_{ij}\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}x_{i}&amp;x_{j}\\
y_{i}&amp;y_{j}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2},\sum_{i&lt;k}a_{ik}\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}x_{i}&amp;x_{k}\\
z_{i}&amp;z_{k}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2},\sum_{j&lt;k}a_{jk}\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}y_{j}&amp;y_{k}\\
z_{j}&amp;z_{k}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2}\Big)\leq\sum_{i&lt;j&lt;k}f(a_{ij},a_{ik},a_{jk})\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}x_{i}&amp;x_{j}&amp;x_{k}\\
y_{i}&amp;y_{j}&amp;y_{k}\\
z_{i}&amp;z_{j}&amp;z_{k}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(34)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In order to prove the above theorem, we shall need the following lemma.</p>
</div>
<div id="ThmThm10" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_Lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="ThmThm10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 10</span></span><span id="ThmThm10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="ThmThm10.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="ThmThm10.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="ThmThm10.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix <math id="ThmThm10.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 3</annotation></semantics></math>. For any symmetric matrix <math id="ThmThm10.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a_{ij})\in\mathbb{M}_{n}({\mathbb{R}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝕄</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ℝ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a_{ij})\in\mathbb{M}_{n}({\mathbb{R}})</annotation></semantics></math> with nonnegative entries and any orthonormal system <math id="ThmThm10.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\textup{{x}},\textup{{y}},\textup{{z}}\}\subset{\mathbb{C}}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\textup{{x}},\textup{{y}},\textup{{z}}\}\subset{\mathbb{C}}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx41" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{i&lt;j&lt;k}\min\{a_{ij},a_{ik},a_{jk}\}\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}x_{i}&amp;x_{j}&amp;x_{k}\\
y_{i}&amp;y_{j}&amp;y_{k}\\
z_{i}&amp;z_{j}&amp;z_{k}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2}\leq\sum_{i&lt;j}a_{ij}\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}x_{i}&amp;x_{j}\\
y_{i}&amp;y_{j}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2}\leq\sum_{i&lt;j&lt;k}\max\{a_{ij},a_{ik},a_{jk}\}\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}x_{i}&amp;x_{j}&amp;x_{k}\\
y_{i}&amp;y_{j}&amp;y_{k}\\
z_{i}&amp;z_{j}&amp;z_{k}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{i&lt;j&lt;k}\min\{a_{ij},a_{ik},a_{jk}\}\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}x_{i}&amp;x_{j}&amp;x_{k}\\
y_{i}&amp;y_{j}&amp;y_{k}\\
z_{i}&amp;z_{j}&amp;z_{k}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2}\leq\sum_{i&lt;j}a_{ij}\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}x_{i}&amp;x_{j}\\
y_{i}&amp;y_{j}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2}\leq\sum_{i&lt;j&lt;k}\max\{a_{ij},a_{ik},a_{jk}\}\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}x_{i}&amp;x_{j}&amp;x_{k}\\
y_{i}&amp;y_{j}&amp;y_{k}\\
z_{i}&amp;z_{j}&amp;z_{k}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(35)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Fix the orthonormal system <math id="S3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\textup{{x}},\textup{{y}},\textup{{z}}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\textup{{x}},\textup{{y}},\textup{{z}}\}</annotation></semantics></math> and, without loss of generality, assume that <math id="S3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{ii}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{ii}=0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>. Observe, crucially, that both inequalities in (<a href="#S3.E35" title="In Lemma 10. ‣ 3 A certain convexity result and the proof of the triangle inequality ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">35</span></a>) are <em id="S3.p3.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">piecewise-linear</em> with respect to <math id="S3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textup{{a}}\vcentcolon=(a_{ij})_{i&lt;j}\in{\mathbb{R}}_{+}^{\binom{n}{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">a</mtext><mo>:=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textup{{a}}\vcentcolon=(a_{ij})_{i&lt;j}\in{\mathbb{R}}_{+}^{\binom{n}{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>. More specifically, let us partition the nonnegative <math id="S3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\binom{n}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\binom{n}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>-orthant <math id="S3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{R}}_{\geq 0}^{\binom{n}{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{R}}_{\geq 0}^{\binom{n}{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> into <math id="S3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\binom{n}{2}!" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\binom{n}{2}!</annotation></semantics></math> regions <math id="S3.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\sigma}</annotation></semantics></math> (where <math id="S3.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> runs over <math id="S3.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{\binom{n}{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{\binom{n}{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>) defined as</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx42" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle C_{\sigma}\vcentcolon=\{\mathbf{P}_{\sigma}\textup{{a}}\in{\mathbb{R}}_{\geq 0}^{\binom{n}{2}}\,|\,a_{12}\geq a_{13}\geq\ldots\geq a_{n-1,n}\geq 0\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">a</mtext></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>12</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>13</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle C_{\sigma}\vcentcolon=\{\mathbf{P}_{\sigma}\textup{{a}}\in{\mathbb{R}}_{\geq 0}^{\binom{n}{2}}\,|\,a_{12}\geq a_{13}\geq\ldots\geq a_{n-1,n}\geq 0\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="S3.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{P}_{\sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{P}_{\sigma}</annotation></semantics></math> is the permutation matrix representing <math id="S3.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma\in S_{\binom{n}{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma\in S_{\binom{n}{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then on each region <math id="S3.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\sigma}</annotation></semantics></math> inequalities (<a href="#S3.E35" title="In Lemma 10. ‣ 3 A certain convexity result and the proof of the triangle inequality ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">35</span></a>) become linear, because for every <math id="S3.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i&lt;j&lt;k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i&lt;j&lt;k</annotation></semantics></math> both the minimum on the left-hand side and the maximum on the right-hand side are determined by the region-specific ordering of the components of <span id="S3.p3.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_bold">a</span>. Notice, moreover, that each region <math id="S3.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\sigma}</annotation></semantics></math> is actually a <em id="S3.p3.2.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">polyhedral cone</em>, and hence it is generated by finitely many vectors <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">15</a>, Corollary 1.3.13]</cite>. Therefore, proving that a linear inequality holds on <math id="S3.p3.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\sigma}</annotation></semantics></math> amounts to veryfing it on its generators, which can be chosen to be the following <math id="S3.p3.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\binom{n}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\binom{n}{2}</annotation></semantics></math> zero-one vectors</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx43" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{P}_{\sigma}[\underbrace{1,\ldots,1}_{k},\underbrace{0,\ldots,0}_{\binom{n}{2}-k}]^{\top},\quad k=1,\ldots,\binom{n}{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mi>k</mi></munder><mo>,</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></munder></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{P}_{\sigma}[\underbrace{1,\ldots,1}_{k},\underbrace{0,\ldots,0}_{\binom{n}{2}-k}]^{\top},\quad k=1,\ldots,\binom{n}{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">Bearing in mind that <math id="S3.p3.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> runs over all permutations, the above observations can be summarized as follows: <em id="S3.p3.3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">In order to prove (<a href="#S3.E35" title="In Lemma 10. ‣ 3 A certain convexity result and the proof of the triangle inequality ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">35</span></a>), <math id="S3.p3.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a_{ij})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a_{ij})</annotation></semantics></math> can be assumed to be a zero-one matrix</em>. This means that, if we introduce <math id="S3.p3.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}\vcentcolon=\{\{i,j\}\,|\,a_{ij}=1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}\vcentcolon=\{\{i,j\}\,|\,a_{ij}=1\}</annotation></semantics></math>, it suffices to prove</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx44" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}i&lt;j&lt;k\\
\{i,j\},\{i,k\},\{j,k\}\in\mathcal{S}\end{subarray}}\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}x_{i}&amp;x_{j}&amp;x_{k}\\
y_{i}&amp;y_{j}&amp;y_{k}\\
z_{i}&amp;z_{j}&amp;z_{k}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2}\leq\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}i&lt;j\\
\{i,j\}\in\mathcal{S}\end{subarray}}\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}x_{i}&amp;x_{j}\\
y_{i}&amp;y_{j}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2}\leq\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}i&lt;j&lt;k\\
\{i,j\}\in\mathcal{S}\,\vee\,\{i,k\}\in\mathcal{S}\,\vee\,\{j,k\}\in\mathcal{S}\end{subarray}}\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}x_{i}&amp;x_{j}&amp;x_{k}\\
y_{i}&amp;y_{j}&amp;y_{k}\\
z_{i}&amp;z_{j}&amp;z_{k}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo lspace="0.392em" rspace="0.392em">∨</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo lspace="0.392em" rspace="0.392em">∨</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}i&lt;j&lt;k\\
\{i,j\},\{i,k\},\{j,k\}\in\mathcal{S}\end{subarray}}\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}x_{i}&amp;x_{j}&amp;x_{k}\\
y_{i}&amp;y_{j}&amp;y_{k}\\
z_{i}&amp;z_{j}&amp;z_{k}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2}\leq\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}i&lt;j\\
\{i,j\}\in\mathcal{S}\end{subarray}}\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}x_{i}&amp;x_{j}\\
y_{i}&amp;y_{j}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2}\leq\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}i&lt;j&lt;k\\
\{i,j\}\in\mathcal{S}\,\vee\,\{i,k\}\in\mathcal{S}\,\vee\,\{j,k\}\in\mathcal{S}\end{subarray}}\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}x_{i}&amp;x_{j}&amp;x_{k}\\
y_{i}&amp;y_{j}&amp;y_{k}\\
z_{i}&amp;z_{j}&amp;z_{k}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(36)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let us focus on the first inequality. It is worthwile to express it in the language of exterior algebra<span id="footnote8" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">8</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">8</sup>
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">8</span>
                
                
                
              The wedge product of <math id="footnote8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> vectors is defined here as <math id="footnote8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{v}_{1}\wedge\ldots\wedge\mathbf{v}_{k}\vcentcolon=\frac{1}{\sqrt{k!}}\sum_{\sigma\in S_{k}}\sgn\sigma\ \mathbf{v}_{\sigma_{1}}\otimes\ldots\otimes\mathbf{v}_{\sigma_{k}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∧</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>∧</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow></msqrt></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>sgn</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}_{1}\wedge\ldots\wedge\mathbf{v}_{k}\vcentcolon=\frac{1}{\sqrt{k!}}\sum_{\sigma\in S_{k}}\sgn\sigma\ \mathbf{v}_{\sigma_{1}}\otimes\ldots\otimes\mathbf{v}_{\sigma_{k}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span></span>. To this end, define the projection operators <math id="S3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P\in\mathcal{B}(\Lambda^{2}\mathbb{C}^{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P\in\mathcal{B}(\Lambda^{2}\mathbb{C}^{n})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q\in\mathcal{B}(\Lambda^{3}\mathbb{C}^{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q\in\mathcal{B}(\Lambda^{3}\mathbb{C}^{n})</annotation></semantics></math> via</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx45" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle P\vcentcolon=\sum_{i&lt;j}\chi_{ij}|\mathbf{e}_{i}\wedge\mathbf{e}_{j}\rangle\langle\mathbf{e}_{i}\wedge\mathbf{e}_{j}|,\qquad Q\vcentcolon=\sum_{i&lt;j&lt;k}\chi_{ij}\chi_{ik}\chi_{jk}|\mathbf{e}_{i}\wedge\mathbf{e}_{j}\wedge\mathbf{e}_{k}\rangle\langle\mathbf{e}_{i}\wedge\mathbf{e}_{j}\wedge\mathbf{e}_{k}|," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∧</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∧</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>χ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>χ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∧</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∧</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∧</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∧</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle P\vcentcolon=\sum_{i&lt;j}\chi_{ij}|\mathbf{e}_{i}\wedge\mathbf{e}_{j}\rangle\langle\mathbf{e}_{i}\wedge\mathbf{e}_{j}|,\qquad Q\vcentcolon=\sum_{i&lt;j&lt;k}\chi_{ij}\chi_{ik}\chi_{jk}|\mathbf{e}_{i}\wedge\mathbf{e}_{j}\wedge\mathbf{e}_{k}\rangle\langle\mathbf{e}_{i}\wedge\mathbf{e}_{j}\wedge\mathbf{e}_{k}|,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="S3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi_{ij}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi_{ij}=1</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{i,j\}\in\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{i,j\}\in\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> otherwise. The first inequality in (<a href="#S3.E36" title="In Proof. ‣ 3 A certain convexity result and the proof of the triangle inequality ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">36</span></a>) is now nothing but</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx46" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|Q(\textup{{x}}\wedge\textup{{y}}\wedge\textup{{z}})\|^{2}\leq\|P(\textup{{x}}\wedge\textup{{y}})\|^{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo>∧</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo>∧</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo>∧</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|Q(\textup{{x}}\wedge\textup{{y}}\wedge\textup{{z}})\|^{2}\leq\|P(\textup{{x}}\wedge\textup{{y}})\|^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(37)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">and we shall in fact prove a stronger result, namely,</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx47" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\forall\mathbf{v}\in{\mathbb{C}}^{n}\ \forall\mathbf{B}\in\Lambda^{2}\mathbb{C}^{n}\quad\|Q(\mathbf{B}\wedge\mathbf{v})\|^{2}\leq\|P\mathbf{B}\|^{2}\|\mathbf{v}\|^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>𝐯</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>𝐁</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐁</mi><mo>∧</mo><mi>𝐯</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐁</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐯</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\forall\mathbf{v}\in{\mathbb{C}}^{n}\ \forall\mathbf{B}\in\Lambda^{2}\mathbb{C}^{n}\quad\|Q(\mathbf{B}\wedge\mathbf{v})\|^{2}\leq\|P\mathbf{B}\|^{2}\|\mathbf{v}\|^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(38)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">Indeed, one has that</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx48" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{B}\wedge\mathbf{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐁</mi><mo>∧</mo><mi>𝐯</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{B}\wedge\mathbf{v}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex40.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\Big(\sum_{i&lt;j}B_{ij}\mathbf{e}_{i}\wedge\mathbf{e}_{j}\Big)\wedge\Big(\sum_{k}v_{k}\mathbf{e}_{k}\Big)=\tfrac{1}{2}\sum_{i,j,k}B_{ij}v_{k}\,\mathbf{e}_{i}\wedge\mathbf{e}_{j}\wedge\mathbf{e}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>∧</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>k</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>∧</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∧</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Big(\sum_{i&lt;j}B_{ij}\mathbf{e}_{i}\wedge\mathbf{e}_{j}\Big)\wedge\Big(\sum_{k}v_{k}\mathbf{e}_{k}\Big)=\tfrac{1}{2}\sum_{i,j,k}B_{ij}v_{k}\,\mathbf{e}_{i}\wedge\mathbf{e}_{j}\wedge\mathbf{e}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i&lt;j&lt;k}(B_{ij}v_{k}-B_{ik}v_{j}+B_{jk}v_{i})\,\mathbf{e}_{i}\wedge\mathbf{e}_{j}\wedge\mathbf{e}_{k}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>∧</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∧</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i&lt;j&lt;k}(B_{ij}v_{k}-B_{ik}v_{j}+B_{jk}v_{i})\,\mathbf{e}_{i}\wedge\mathbf{e}_{j}\wedge\mathbf{e}_{k},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p4.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p4.5.1" class="ltx_text">and hence</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx49" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|Q(\mathbf{B}\wedge\mathbf{v})\|^{2}=\sum_{i&lt;j&lt;k}\chi_{ij}\chi_{ik}\chi_{jk}|B_{ij}v_{k}-B_{ik}v_{j}+B_{jk}v_{i}|^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐁</mi><mo>∧</mo><mi>𝐯</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>χ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>χ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|Q(\mathbf{B}\wedge\mathbf{v})\|^{2}=\sum_{i&lt;j&lt;k}\chi_{ij}\chi_{ik}\chi_{jk}|B_{ij}v_{k}-B_{ik}v_{j}+B_{jk}v_{i}|^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(39)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p4.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p4.6.1" class="ltx_text">On the other hand, one has that</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx50" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle P(\mathbf{B})\wedge\mathbf{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐁</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mi>𝐯</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle P(\mathbf{B})\wedge\mathbf{v}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex42.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\Big(\sum_{i&lt;j}\chi_{ij}B_{ij}\mathbf{e}_{i}\wedge\mathbf{e}_{j}\Big)\wedge\Big(\sum_{k}v_{k}\mathbf{e}_{k}\Big)=\tfrac{1}{2}\sum_{i,j,k}\chi_{ij}B_{ij}v_{k}\,\mathbf{e}_{i}\wedge\mathbf{e}_{j}\wedge\mathbf{e}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>∧</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>k</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>∧</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∧</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Big(\sum_{i&lt;j}\chi_{ij}B_{ij}\mathbf{e}_{i}\wedge\mathbf{e}_{j}\Big)\wedge\Big(\sum_{k}v_{k}\mathbf{e}_{k}\Big)=\tfrac{1}{2}\sum_{i,j,k}\chi_{ij}B_{ij}v_{k}\,\mathbf{e}_{i}\wedge\mathbf{e}_{j}\wedge\mathbf{e}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i&lt;j&lt;k}(\chi_{ij}B_{ij}v_{k}-\chi_{ik}B_{ik}v_{j}+\chi_{jk}B_{jk}v_{i})\,\mathbf{e}_{i}\wedge\mathbf{e}_{j}\wedge\mathbf{e}_{k}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>∧</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∧</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i&lt;j&lt;k}(\chi_{ij}B_{ij}v_{k}-\chi_{ik}B_{ik}v_{j}+\chi_{jk}B_{jk}v_{i})\,\mathbf{e}_{i}\wedge\mathbf{e}_{j}\wedge\mathbf{e}_{k},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p4.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p4.7.1" class="ltx_text">and hence</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx51" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|P(\mathbf{B})\wedge\mathbf{v}\|^{2}=\sum_{i&lt;j&lt;k}|\chi_{ij}B_{ij}v_{k}-\chi_{ik}B_{ik}v_{j}+\chi_{jk}B_{jk}v_{i}|^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐁</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mi>𝐯</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|P(\mathbf{B})\wedge\mathbf{v}\|^{2}=\sum_{i&lt;j&lt;k}|\chi_{ij}B_{ij}v_{k}-\chi_{ik}B_{ik}v_{j}+\chi_{jk}B_{jk}v_{i}|^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(40)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p4.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p4.8.1" class="ltx_text">But since <math id="S3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi_{ij}\chi_{ik}\chi_{jk}|B_{ij}v_{k}-B_{ik}v_{j}+B_{jk}v_{i}|^{2}\leq|\chi_{ij}B_{ij}v_{k}-\chi_{ik}B_{ik}v_{j}+\chi_{jk}B_{jk}v_{i}|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>χ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>χ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi_{ij}\chi_{ik}\chi_{jk}|B_{ij}v_{k}-B_{ik}v_{j}+B_{jk}v_{i}|^{2}\leq|\chi_{ij}B_{ij}v_{k}-\chi_{ik}B_{ik}v_{j}+\chi_{jk}B_{jk}v_{i}|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="S3.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i,j,k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i,j,k</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain that <math id="S3.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|Q(\mathbf{B}\wedge\mathbf{v})\|^{2}\leq\|P(\mathbf{B})\wedge\mathbf{v}\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐁</mi><mo>∧</mo><mi>𝐯</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐁</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mi>𝐯</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|Q(\mathbf{B}\wedge\mathbf{v})\|^{2}\leq\|P(\mathbf{B})\wedge\mathbf{v}\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, what in turn can be bounded from above by <math id="S3.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|P\mathbf{B}\|^{2}\|\mathbf{v}\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐁</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐯</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|P\mathbf{B}\|^{2}\|\mathbf{v}\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, for instance on the strength of the identity<span id="footnote9" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">9</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">9</sup>
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">9</span>
                
                
                
              This generalization of the Lagrange identity can be easily proven by direct calculation in an orthonormal basis of <math id="footnote9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{C}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{C}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> containing <math id="footnote9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{w}/\|\mathbf{w}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐰</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{w}/\|\mathbf{w}\|</annotation></semantics></math> as its first element.</span></span></span></span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx52" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\forall\mathbf{w}\in\mathbb{C}^{n}\ \forall\boldsymbol{\Omega}\in\Lambda^{k}\mathbb{C}^{n}\quad\|\mathbf{w}\wedge\boldsymbol{\Omega}\|^{2}=\|\mathbf{w}\|^{2}\|\boldsymbol{\Omega}\|^{2}-\|\mathbf{w}\lrcorner\,\boldsymbol{\Omega}\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>𝐰</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>𝛀</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>∧</mo><mi>𝛀</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐰</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝛀</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐰</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">⌟</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝛀</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\forall\mathbf{w}\in\mathbb{C}^{n}\ \forall\boldsymbol{\Omega}\in\Lambda^{k}\mathbb{C}^{n}\quad\|\mathbf{w}\wedge\boldsymbol{\Omega}\|^{2}=\|\mathbf{w}\|^{2}\|\boldsymbol{\Omega}\|^{2}-\|\mathbf{w}\lrcorner\,\boldsymbol{\Omega}\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p4.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p4.9.1" class="ltx_text">for any <math id="S3.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in\{1,\ldots,n\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in\{1,\ldots,n\}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S3.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lrcorner" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">⌟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lrcorner</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the interior product, defined on simple <math id="S3.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-vectors via <math id="S3.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{w}\lrcorner\,(\mathbf{v}_{1}\wedge\ldots\wedge\mathbf{v}_{k})=\sum_{i}(-1)^{i-1}\langle\mathbf{w}|\mathbf{v}_{i}\rangle\mathbf{v}_{1}\wedge\ldots\wedge\widehat{\mathbf{v}}_{i}\wedge\ldots\wedge\mathbf{v}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐰</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">⌟</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∧</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>∧</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>𝐰</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>∧</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∧</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>∧</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{w}\lrcorner\,(\mathbf{v}_{1}\wedge\ldots\wedge\mathbf{v}_{k})=\sum_{i}(-1)^{i-1}\langle\mathbf{w}|\mathbf{v}_{i}\rangle\mathbf{v}_{1}\wedge\ldots\wedge\widehat{\mathbf{v}}_{i}\wedge\ldots\wedge\mathbf{v}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. This completes the proof of (<a href="#S3.E38" title="In Proof. ‣ 3 A certain convexity result and the proof of the triangle inequality ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">38</span></a>) and thus of the first inequality in (<a href="#S3.E36" title="In Proof. ‣ 3 A certain convexity result and the proof of the triangle inequality ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">36</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">As for the second inequality, observe that, by the Cauchy–Binet theorem and by the orthonormality of <math id="S3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\textup{{x}},\textup{{y}},\textup{{z}}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\textup{{x}},\textup{{y}},\textup{{z}}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, it can be equivalently written as</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx53" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 1-\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}i&lt;j\\
\{i,j\}\in\mathcal{S}^{c}\end{subarray}}\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}x_{i}&amp;x_{j}\\
y_{i}&amp;y_{j}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2}\leq 1-\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}i&lt;j&lt;k\\
\{i,j\},\{i,k\},\{j,k\}\in\mathcal{S}^{c}\end{subarray}}\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}x_{i}&amp;x_{j}&amp;x_{k}\\
y_{i}&amp;y_{j}&amp;y_{k}\\
z_{i}&amp;z_{j}&amp;z_{k}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>c</mi></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>c</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 1-\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}i&lt;j\\
\{i,j\}\in\mathcal{S}^{c}\end{subarray}}\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}x_{i}&amp;x_{j}\\
y_{i}&amp;y_{j}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2}\leq 1-\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}i&lt;j&lt;k\\
\{i,j\},\{i,k\},\{j,k\}\in\mathcal{S}^{c}\end{subarray}}\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}x_{i}&amp;x_{j}&amp;x_{k}\\
y_{i}&amp;y_{j}&amp;y_{k}\\
z_{i}&amp;z_{j}&amp;z_{k}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">and since the subset of pairs <math id="S3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math> was arbitrary, the above inequality follows from the one already proven. This concludes the proof on the entire lemma.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Theorem <a href="#ThmThm9" title="Theorem 9. ‣ 3 A certain convexity result and the proof of the triangle inequality ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="S3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let us first introduce some convenient notation. Define</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx54" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{g}\vcentcolon=\Big(\sum_{i&lt;j}a_{ij}\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}x_{i}&amp;x_{j}\\
y_{i}&amp;y_{j}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2},\sum_{i&lt;k}a_{ik}\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}x_{i}&amp;x_{k}\\
z_{i}&amp;z_{k}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2},\sum_{j&lt;k}a_{jk}\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}y_{j}&amp;y_{k}\\
z_{j}&amp;z_{k}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2}\Big)\in\mathbb{R}^{3}_{\geq 0}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐠</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{g}\vcentcolon=\Big(\sum_{i&lt;j}a_{ij}\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}x_{i}&amp;x_{j}\\
y_{i}&amp;y_{j}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2},\sum_{i&lt;k}a_{ik}\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}x_{i}&amp;x_{k}\\
z_{i}&amp;z_{k}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2},\sum_{j&lt;k}a_{jk}\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}y_{j}&amp;y_{k}\\
z_{j}&amp;z_{k}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2}\Big)\in\mathbb{R}^{3}_{\geq 0},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">so that the left-hand side of our desired inequality (<a href="#S3.E34" title="In Theorem 9. ‣ 3 A certain convexity result and the proof of the triangle inequality ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">34</span></a>) becomes simply <math id="S3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(\mathbf{g})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐠</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\mathbf{g})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let us introduce the set of ordered triples <math id="S3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}_{3}\vcentcolon=\{(i,j,k)\ |\ 1\leq i&lt;j&lt;k\leq n\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo rspace="0.222em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}_{3}\vcentcolon=\{(i,j,k)\ |\ 1\leq i&lt;j&lt;k\leq n\}</annotation></semantics></math> and, for any <math id="S3.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\vcentcolon=(i,j,k)\in\mathcal{O}_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\vcentcolon=(i,j,k)\in\mathcal{O}_{3}</annotation></semantics></math>, let us denote <math id="S3.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{t}\vcentcolon=\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}x_{i}&amp;x_{j}&amp;x_{k}\\
y_{i}&amp;y_{j}&amp;y_{k}\\
z_{i}&amp;z_{j}&amp;z_{k}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t}\vcentcolon=\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}x_{i}&amp;x_{j}&amp;x_{k}\\
y_{i}&amp;y_{j}&amp;y_{k}\\
z_{i}&amp;z_{j}&amp;z_{k}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Notice that this defines a probability distribution on <math id="S3.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}_{3}</annotation></semantics></math>, because <math id="S3.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{t}p_{t}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{t}p_{t}=1</annotation></semantics></math> by the orthonormality of <math id="S3.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\textup{{x}},\textup{{y}},\textup{{z}}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\textup{{x}},\textup{{y}},\textup{{z}}\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">For any ordered triple <math id="S3.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\vcentcolon=(i,j,k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\vcentcolon=(i,j,k)</annotation></semantics></math> define <math id="S3.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textup{{a}}_{t}\vcentcolon=(a_{ij},a_{ik},a_{jk})\in{\mathbb{R}}^{3}_{\geq 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">a</mtext><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textup{{a}}_{t}\vcentcolon=(a_{ij},a_{ik},a_{jk})\in{\mathbb{R}}^{3}_{\geq 0}</annotation></semantics></math> and observe that the right-hand side of our desired inequality (<a href="#S3.E34" title="In Theorem 9. ‣ 3 A certain convexity result and the proof of the triangle inequality ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">34</span></a>) is nothing but <math id="S3.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{t}p_{t}f(\textup{{a}}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">a</mtext><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{t}p_{t}f(\textup{{a}}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">The crucial step is to prove that it is always possible to find a family of <math id="S3.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3\times 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3\times 3</annotation></semantics></math> doubly stochastic matrices <math id="S3.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathbf{Q}_{t}\}_{t\in T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathbf{Q}_{t}\}_{t\in T}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx55" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{t}p_{t}\mathbf{Q}_{t}\textup{{a}}_{t}=\mathbf{g}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>t</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">a</mtext><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐠</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{t}p_{t}\mathbf{Q}_{t}\textup{{a}}_{t}=\mathbf{g}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(41)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">If we manage to prove the above claim, inequality (<a href="#S3.E34" title="In Theorem 9. ‣ 3 A certain convexity result and the proof of the triangle inequality ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">34</span></a>) would then easily follow. Indeed, since by the Birkhoff–von Neumann theorem every <math id="S3.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Q}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Q}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is a convex combination of permutation matrices <math id="S3.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{P}_{\sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{P}_{\sigma}</annotation></semantics></math>, we would have</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx56" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f(\mathbf{g})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐠</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f(\mathbf{g})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex47.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=f\Big(\sum\nolimits_{t}p_{t}\mathbf{Q}_{t}\textup{{a}}_{t}\Big)=f\Big(\sum\nolimits_{t}p_{t}\sum\nolimits_{\sigma\in S_{3}}\lambda_{t,\sigma}\mathbf{P}_{\sigma}\textup{{a}}_{t}\Big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>t</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">a</mtext><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>t</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></msub></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">a</mtext><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=f\Big(\sum\nolimits_{t}p_{t}\mathbf{Q}_{t}\textup{{a}}_{t}\Big)=f\Big(\sum\nolimits_{t}p_{t}\sum\nolimits_{\sigma\in S_{3}}\lambda_{t,\sigma}\mathbf{P}_{\sigma}\textup{{a}}_{t}\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\sum\nolimits_{t}p_{t}\sum\nolimits_{\sigma\in S_{3}}\lambda_{t,\sigma}f\big(\mathbf{P}_{\sigma}\textup{{a}}_{t}\big)=\sum\nolimits_{t}p_{t}\sum\nolimits_{\sigma\in S_{3}}\lambda_{t,\sigma}f(\textup{{a}}_{t})=\sum\nolimits_{t}p_{t}f(\textup{{a}}_{t})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>t</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></msub></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">a</mtext><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>t</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></msub></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">a</mtext><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>t</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">a</mtext><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\sum\nolimits_{t}p_{t}\sum\nolimits_{\sigma\in S_{3}}\lambda_{t,\sigma}f\big(\mathbf{P}_{\sigma}\textup{{a}}_{t}\big)=\sum\nolimits_{t}p_{t}\sum\nolimits_{\sigma\in S_{3}}\lambda_{t,\sigma}f(\textup{{a}}_{t})=\sum\nolimits_{t}p_{t}f(\textup{{a}}_{t}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p9.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p9.3.1" class="ltx_text">where we have used (<a href="#S3.E41" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ 3 A certain convexity result and the proof of the triangle inequality ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">41</span></a>), Birkhoff–von Neumann theorem, Jensen’s inequality by the joint convexity of <math id="S3.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>, the total symmetricity of <math id="S3.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> and, in the final equality, we simply summed over <math id="S3.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> the convex combination coefficients <math id="S3.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{t,\sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{t,\sigma}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">In order to prove the claim, observe that (<a href="#S3.E41" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ 3 A certain convexity result and the proof of the triangle inequality ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">41</span></a>) can be restated as saying that <math id="S3.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐠</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{g}</annotation></semantics></math> belongs to the following Minkowski combination of compact convex sets</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx57" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex49"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{g}\in\mathcal{K}\vcentcolon=\sum_{t}p_{t}\{\mathbf{Q}\textup{{a}}_{t}\,|\,\mathbf{Q}\in\mathcal{B}_{3}\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐠</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>t</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>𝐐</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">a</mtext><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{g}\in\mathcal{K}\vcentcolon=\sum_{t}p_{t}\{\mathbf{Q}\textup{{a}}_{t}\,|\,\mathbf{Q}\in\mathcal{B}_{3}\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="S3.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{3}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the Birkhoff polytope of <math id="S3.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math>-by-<math id="S3.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math> doubly stochastic matrices. But since <math id="S3.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{K}</annotation></semantics></math> is thus compact and convex itself, the condition <math id="S3.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{g}\in\mathcal{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐠</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{g}\in\mathcal{K}</annotation></semantics></math> in turn can be equivalently expressed via its support function<span id="footnote10" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">10</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">10</sup>
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">10</span>
                
                
                
              See e.g. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">19</a>]</cite> for the exposition of support functions’ basic properties.</span></span></span> <math id="S3.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\mathcal{K}}(\mathbf{w})\vcentcolon=\sup_{\mathbf{u}\in\mathcal{K}}\mathbf{w}^{\top}\mathbf{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐰</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>𝐮</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msup><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐮</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\mathcal{K}}(\mathbf{w})\vcentcolon=\sup_{\mathbf{u}\in\mathcal{K}}\mathbf{w}^{\top}\mathbf{u}</annotation></semantics></math> as</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx58" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex50"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\forall\mathbf{w}\in{\mathbb{R}}^{3}\quad\mathbf{w}^{\top}\mathbf{g}\leq h_{\mathcal{K}}(\mathbf{w})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>𝐰</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐠</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐰</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\forall\mathbf{w}\in{\mathbb{R}}^{3}\quad\mathbf{w}^{\top}\mathbf{g}\leq h_{\mathcal{K}}(\mathbf{w}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p10.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p10.3.1" class="ltx_text">Since support functions of compact convex sets satisfy <math id="S3.p10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\lambda\mathcal{C}}=\lambda h_{\mathcal{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\lambda\mathcal{C}}=\lambda h_{\mathcal{C}}</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="S3.p10.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> and are Minkowski additive <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">19</a>, Theorem 1.7.5]</cite>, the function <math id="S3.p10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\mathcal{K}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\mathcal{K}}</annotation></semantics></math> can be expressed as</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx59" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex51"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle h_{\mathcal{K}}(\mathbf{w})=\sum_{t}p_{t}\sup_{Q\in\mathcal{B}_{3}}\mathbf{w}^{\top}\mathbf{Q}\textup{{a}}_{t}=\sum_{t}p_{t}\max_{\sigma\in S_{3}}\,\mathbf{w}^{\top}\mathbf{P}_{\sigma}\textup{{a}}_{t}=\sum_{t}p_{t}(\mathbf{w}^{\downarrow})^{\top}\textup{{a}}^{\downarrow}_{t}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐰</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>t</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><msup><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐐</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">a</mtext><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>t</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">a</mtext><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>t</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐰</mi><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">a</mtext><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle h_{\mathcal{K}}(\mathbf{w})=\sum_{t}p_{t}\sup_{Q\in\mathcal{B}_{3}}\mathbf{w}^{\top}\mathbf{Q}\textup{{a}}_{t}=\sum_{t}p_{t}\max_{\sigma\in S_{3}}\,\mathbf{w}^{\top}\mathbf{P}_{\sigma}\textup{{a}}_{t}=\sum_{t}p_{t}(\mathbf{w}^{\downarrow})^{\top}\textup{{a}}^{\downarrow}_{t},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p10.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p10.4.1" class="ltx_text">where in the second equality we have used the fact that the supremum of the linear map <math id="S3.p10.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{3}\ni\mathbf{Q}\mapsto\mathbf{w}^{\top}\mathbf{Q}\textup{{a}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>∋</mo><mi>𝐐</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐐</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">a</mtext><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{3}\ni\mathbf{Q}\mapsto\mathbf{w}^{\top}\mathbf{Q}\textup{{a}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> must be attained at one of the extreme points of <math id="S3.p10.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{3}</annotation></semantics></math>—which by the Birkhoff–von Neumann theorem are precisely the permutation matrices—and the third equality simply picks the rearrangement maximum for every <math id="S3.p10.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in\mathcal{O}_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in\mathcal{O}_{3}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">But since <math id="S3.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{w}^{\top}\mathbf{g}\leq(\mathbf{w}^{\downarrow})^{\top}\mathbf{g}^{\downarrow}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐠</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐰</mi><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐠</mi><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{w}^{\top}\mathbf{g}\leq(\mathbf{w}^{\downarrow})^{\top}\mathbf{g}^{\downarrow}</annotation></semantics></math> by the rearrangement inequality, we can restrict our attention to the set <math id="S3.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\vcentcolon=\{\mathbf{w}\in{\mathbb{R}}^{3}\,|\,w_{1}\geq w_{2}\geq w_{3}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\vcentcolon=\{\mathbf{w}\in{\mathbb{R}}^{3}\,|\,w_{1}\geq w_{2}\geq w_{3}\}</annotation></semantics></math> and prove the <em id="S3.p11.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">linear</em> inequality</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx60" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\forall\mathbf{w}\in C\quad\mathbf{w}^{\top}\mathbf{g}^{\downarrow}\leq\sum_{t}p_{t}\mathbf{w}^{\top}\textup{{a}}^{\downarrow}_{t}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>𝐰</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐠</mi><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>t</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">a</mtext><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\forall\mathbf{w}\in C\quad\mathbf{w}^{\top}\mathbf{g}^{\downarrow}\leq\sum_{t}p_{t}\mathbf{w}^{\top}\textup{{a}}^{\downarrow}_{t}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(42)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p11.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p11.2.1" class="ltx_text">In fact, since <math id="S3.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> is a finitely generated cone (cf. the proof of Lemma <a href="#ThmThm10" title="Lemma 10. ‣ 3 A certain convexity result and the proof of the triangle inequality ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> above), it suffices to prove (<a href="#S3.E42" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ 3 A certain convexity result and the proof of the triangle inequality ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">42</span></a>) on its generators, which can be chosen to be <math id="S3.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{w}_{1}\vcentcolon=[1,1,1]^{\top},\mathbf{w}_{2}\vcentcolon=[1,0,0]^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐰</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐰</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{w}_{1}\vcentcolon=[1,1,1]^{\top},\mathbf{w}_{2}\vcentcolon=[1,0,0]^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{w}_{3}\vcentcolon=[0,0,-1]^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐰</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{w}_{3}\vcentcolon=[0,0,-1]^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">On <math id="S3.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{w}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐰</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{w}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> (<a href="#S3.E42" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ 3 A certain convexity result and the proof of the triangle inequality ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">42</span></a>) is in fact an <em id="S3.p12.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">equality</em>. Indeed, by changing the dummy indices’ names, moving between the ordered and unordered sums, and making use of the symmetries of <math id="S3.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a_{ij})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a_{ij})</annotation></semantics></math> and of the minors, one can write that</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx61" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex52"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{w}_{1}^{\top}\mathbf{g}^{\downarrow}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐰</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐠</mi><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{w}_{1}^{\top}\mathbf{g}^{\downarrow}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex52.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i&lt;j}a_{ij}\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}x_{i}&amp;x_{j}\\
y_{i}&amp;y_{j}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2}+\sum_{i&lt;k}a_{ik}\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}x_{i}&amp;x_{k}\\
z_{i}&amp;z_{k}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2}+\sum_{j&lt;k}a_{jk}\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}y_{j}&amp;y_{k}\\
z_{j}&amp;z_{k}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i&lt;j}a_{ij}\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}x_{i}&amp;x_{j}\\
y_{i}&amp;y_{j}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2}+\sum_{i&lt;k}a_{ik}\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}x_{i}&amp;x_{k}\\
z_{i}&amp;z_{k}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2}+\sum_{j&lt;k}a_{jk}\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}y_{j}&amp;y_{k}\\
z_{j}&amp;z_{k}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex53"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\tfrac{1}{2}\sum_{i,j}a_{ij}\left(\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}x_{i}&amp;x_{j}\\
y_{i}&amp;y_{j}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2}+\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}x_{i}&amp;x_{j}\\
z_{i}&amp;z_{j}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2}+\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}y_{i}&amp;y_{j}\\
z_{i}&amp;z_{j}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2}\right)=\tfrac{1}{2}\sum_{i,j,k}a_{ij}\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}x_{i}&amp;x_{j}&amp;x_{k}\\
y_{i}&amp;y_{j}&amp;y_{k}\\
z_{i}&amp;z_{j}&amp;z_{k}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\tfrac{1}{2}\sum_{i,j}a_{ij}\left(\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}x_{i}&amp;x_{j}\\
y_{i}&amp;y_{j}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2}+\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}x_{i}&amp;x_{j}\\
z_{i}&amp;z_{j}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2}+\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}y_{i}&amp;y_{j}\\
z_{i}&amp;z_{j}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2}\right)=\tfrac{1}{2}\sum_{i,j,k}a_{ij}\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}x_{i}&amp;x_{j}&amp;x_{k}\\
y_{i}&amp;y_{j}&amp;y_{k}\\
z_{i}&amp;z_{j}&amp;z_{k}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex54"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\tfrac{1}{6}\sum_{i,j,k}\left(a_{ij}+a_{ik}+a_{jk}\right)\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}x_{i}&amp;x_{j}&amp;x_{k}\\
y_{i}&amp;y_{j}&amp;y_{k}\\
z_{i}&amp;z_{j}&amp;z_{k}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2}=\sum_{i&lt;j&lt;k}\left(a_{ij}+a_{ik}+a_{jk}\right)\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}x_{i}&amp;x_{j}&amp;x_{k}\\
y_{i}&amp;y_{j}&amp;y_{k}\\
z_{i}&amp;z_{j}&amp;z_{k}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2}=\sum_{t}p_{t}\mathbf{w}_{1}^{\top}\textup{{a}}^{\downarrow}_{t}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>t</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐰</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">a</mtext><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\tfrac{1}{6}\sum_{i,j,k}\left(a_{ij}+a_{ik}+a_{jk}\right)\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}x_{i}&amp;x_{j}&amp;x_{k}\\
y_{i}&amp;y_{j}&amp;y_{k}\\
z_{i}&amp;z_{j}&amp;z_{k}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2}=\sum_{i&lt;j&lt;k}\left(a_{ij}+a_{ik}+a_{jk}\right)\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}x_{i}&amp;x_{j}&amp;x_{k}\\
y_{i}&amp;y_{j}&amp;y_{k}\\
z_{i}&amp;z_{j}&amp;z_{k}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2}=\sum_{t}p_{t}\mathbf{w}_{1}^{\top}\textup{{a}}^{\downarrow}_{t}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">On <math id="S3.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{w}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐰</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{w}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> (<a href="#S3.E42" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ 3 A certain convexity result and the proof of the triangle inequality ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">42</span></a>) can be written as</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx62" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex55"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\max\left\{\sum_{i&lt;j}a_{ij}\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}x_{i}&amp;x_{j}\\
y_{i}&amp;y_{j}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2},\sum_{i&lt;k}a_{ik}\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}x_{i}&amp;x_{k}\\
z_{i}&amp;z_{k}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2},\sum_{j&lt;k}a_{jk}\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}y_{j}&amp;y_{k}\\
z_{j}&amp;z_{k}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2}\right\}\leq\sum_{i&lt;j&lt;k}\max\{a_{ij},a_{ik},a_{jk}\}\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}x_{i}&amp;x_{j}&amp;x_{k}\\
y_{i}&amp;y_{j}&amp;y_{k}\\
z_{i}&amp;z_{j}&amp;z_{k}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\max\left\{\sum_{i&lt;j}a_{ij}\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}x_{i}&amp;x_{j}\\
y_{i}&amp;y_{j}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2},\sum_{i&lt;k}a_{ik}\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}x_{i}&amp;x_{k}\\
z_{i}&amp;z_{k}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2},\sum_{j&lt;k}a_{jk}\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}y_{j}&amp;y_{k}\\
z_{j}&amp;z_{k}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2}\right\}\leq\sum_{i&lt;j&lt;k}\max\{a_{ij},a_{ik},a_{jk}\}\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}x_{i}&amp;x_{j}&amp;x_{k}\\
y_{i}&amp;y_{j}&amp;y_{k}\\
z_{i}&amp;z_{j}&amp;z_{k}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p13.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p13.2.1" class="ltx_text">what follows immediately from the second inequality in (<a href="#S3.E35" title="In Lemma 10. ‣ 3 A certain convexity result and the proof of the triangle inequality ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">35</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">Similarly, on <math id="S3.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{w}_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐰</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{w}_{3}</annotation></semantics></math> (<a href="#S3.E42" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ 3 A certain convexity result and the proof of the triangle inequality ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">42</span></a>) boils down to</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx63" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex56"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\min\left\{\sum_{i&lt;j}a_{ij}\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}x_{i}&amp;x_{j}\\
y_{i}&amp;y_{j}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2},\sum_{i&lt;k}a_{ik}\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}x_{i}&amp;x_{k}\\
z_{i}&amp;z_{k}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2},\sum_{j&lt;k}a_{jk}\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}y_{j}&amp;y_{k}\\
z_{j}&amp;z_{k}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2}\right\}\geq\sum_{i&lt;j&lt;k}\min\{a_{ij},a_{ik},a_{jk}\}\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}x_{i}&amp;x_{j}&amp;x_{k}\\
y_{i}&amp;y_{j}&amp;y_{k}\\
z_{i}&amp;z_{j}&amp;z_{k}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\min\left\{\sum_{i&lt;j}a_{ij}\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}x_{i}&amp;x_{j}\\
y_{i}&amp;y_{j}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2},\sum_{i&lt;k}a_{ik}\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}x_{i}&amp;x_{k}\\
z_{i}&amp;z_{k}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2},\sum_{j&lt;k}a_{jk}\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}y_{j}&amp;y_{k}\\
z_{j}&amp;z_{k}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2}\right\}\geq\sum_{i&lt;j&lt;k}\min\{a_{ij},a_{ik},a_{jk}\}\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}x_{i}&amp;x_{j}&amp;x_{k}\\
y_{i}&amp;y_{j}&amp;y_{k}\\
z_{i}&amp;z_{j}&amp;z_{k}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p14.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p14.2.1" class="ltx_text">what follows immediately from the first inequality in (<a href="#S3.E35" title="In Lemma 10. ‣ 3 A certain convexity result and the proof of the triangle inequality ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">35</span></a>). Thus invoking Lemma <a href="#ThmThm10" title="Lemma 10. ‣ 3 A certain convexity result and the proof of the triangle inequality ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> concludes the proof that <math id="S3.p14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{g}\in\mathcal{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐠</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{g}\in\mathcal{K}</annotation></semantics></math> and hence of the entire Theorem.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p15.1" class="ltx_p">By replacing <math id="S3.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S3.p15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-f</annotation></semantics></math> in Theorem <a href="#ThmThm9" title="Theorem 9. ‣ 3 A certain convexity result and the proof of the triangle inequality ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>, we immediately obtain the related concavity result.</p>
</div>
<div id="ThmThm11" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_Cor">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="ThmThm11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary 11</span></span><span id="ThmThm11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="ThmThm11.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="ThmThm11.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="ThmThm11.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix <math id="ThmThm11.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 3</annotation></semantics></math>. For any symmetric matrix <math id="ThmThm11.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a_{ij})\in\mathbb{M}_{n}({\mathbb{R}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝕄</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ℝ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a_{ij})\in\mathbb{M}_{n}({\mathbb{R}})</annotation></semantics></math> with nonnegative entries, any orthonormal system <math id="ThmThm11.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\textup{{x}},\textup{{y}},\textup{{z}}\}\subset{\mathbb{C}}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\textup{{x}},\textup{{y}},\textup{{z}}\}\subset{\mathbb{C}}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> and any jointly concave, completely symmetric map <math id="ThmThm11.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}^{3}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}^{3}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx64" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f\Big(\sum_{i&lt;j}a_{ij}\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}x_{i}&amp;x_{j}\\
y_{i}&amp;y_{j}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2},\sum_{i&lt;k}a_{ik}\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}x_{i}&amp;x_{k}\\
z_{i}&amp;z_{k}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2},\sum_{j&lt;k}a_{jk}\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}y_{j}&amp;y_{k}\\
z_{j}&amp;z_{k}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2}\Big)\geq\sum_{i&lt;j&lt;k}f(a_{ij},a_{ik},a_{jk})\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}x_{i}&amp;x_{j}&amp;x_{k}\\
y_{i}&amp;y_{j}&amp;y_{k}\\
z_{i}&amp;z_{j}&amp;z_{k}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f\Big(\sum_{i&lt;j}a_{ij}\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}x_{i}&amp;x_{j}\\
y_{i}&amp;y_{j}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2},\sum_{i&lt;k}a_{ik}\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}x_{i}&amp;x_{k}\\
z_{i}&amp;z_{k}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2},\sum_{j&lt;k}a_{jk}\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}y_{j}&amp;y_{k}\\
z_{j}&amp;z_{k}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2}\Big)\geq\sum_{i&lt;j&lt;k}f(a_{ij},a_{ik},a_{jk})\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}x_{i}&amp;x_{j}&amp;x_{k}\\
y_{i}&amp;y_{j}&amp;y_{k}\\
z_{i}&amp;z_{j}&amp;z_{k}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(43)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.p16" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p16.1" class="ltx_p">We are now finally ready to prove the triangle inequality for <math id="S3.p16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{p}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Theorem <a href="#ThmThm2" title="Theorem 2. ‣ 1 Introduction and main result ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="S3.p17" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p17.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p17.1.1" class="ltx_text">On the strength of Remark <a href="#ThmThm6" title="Remark 6. ‣ 1 Introduction and main result ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> and Proposition <a href="#ThmThm8" title="Proposition 8. ‣ 2 The 𝑛=3 case and its consequences ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>, it suffices to show (<a href="#S1.E4" title="In Theorem 2. ‣ 1 Introduction and main result ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>) for any fixed orthonormal system <math id="S3.p17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\textup{{x}},\textup{{y}},\textup{{z}}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\textup{{x}},\textup{{y}},\textup{{z}}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, which can be equivalently stated as</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx65" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 2\max\{d_{p}(\textup{{x}},\textup{{y}}),d_{p}(\textup{{x}},\textup{{z}}),d_{p}(\textup{{y}},\textup{{z}})\}\leq d_{p}(\textup{{x}},\textup{{y}})+d_{p}(\textup{{x}},\textup{{z}})+d_{p}(\textup{{y}},\textup{{z}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 2\max\{d_{p}(\textup{{x}},\textup{{y}}),d_{p}(\textup{{x}},\textup{{z}}),d_{p}(\textup{{y}},\textup{{z}})\}\leq d_{p}(\textup{{x}},\textup{{y}})+d_{p}(\textup{{x}},\textup{{z}})+d_{p}(\textup{{y}},\textup{{z}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(44)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p17.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p17.2.1" class="ltx_text">for any orthonormal <math id="S3.p17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\textup{{x}},\textup{{y}},\textup{{z}}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\textup{{x}},\textup{{y}},\textup{{z}}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. To this end, let us write the following chain of (in)equalities</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx66" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex57"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 2^{p}\max\{d^{p}_{p}(\textup{{x}},\textup{{y}}),d^{p}_{p}(\textup{{x}},\textup{{z}}),d^{p}_{p}(\textup{{y}},\textup{{z}})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>p</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>p</mi><mi>p</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>p</mi><mi>p</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>p</mi><mi>p</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 2^{p}\max\{d^{p}_{p}(\textup{{x}},\textup{{y}}),d^{p}_{p}(\textup{{x}},\textup{{z}}),d^{p}_{p}(\textup{{y}},\textup{{z}})\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex58"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=2^{p}\max\left\{\sum_{i&lt;j}E^{p}_{ij}\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}x_{i}&amp;x_{j}\\
y_{i}&amp;y_{j}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2},\sum_{i&lt;k}E^{p}_{ik}\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}x_{i}&amp;x_{k}\\
z_{i}&amp;z_{k}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2},\sum_{j&lt;k}E^{p}_{jk}\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}y_{j}&amp;y_{k}\\
z_{j}&amp;z_{k}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2}\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>p</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>p</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>p</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>p</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=2^{p}\max\left\{\sum_{i&lt;j}E^{p}_{ij}\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}x_{i}&amp;x_{j}\\
y_{i}&amp;y_{j}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2},\sum_{i&lt;k}E^{p}_{ik}\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}x_{i}&amp;x_{k}\\
z_{i}&amp;z_{k}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2},\sum_{j&lt;k}E^{p}_{jk}\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}y_{j}&amp;y_{k}\\
z_{j}&amp;z_{k}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex59"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 2^{p}\sum_{i&lt;j&lt;k}\max(E^{p}_{ij},E^{p}_{ik},E^{p}_{jk})\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}x_{i}&amp;x_{j}&amp;x_{k}\\
y_{i}&amp;y_{j}&amp;y_{k}\\
z_{i}&amp;z_{j}&amp;z_{k}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2}\leq\sum_{i&lt;j&lt;k}(E_{ij}+E_{ik}+E_{jk})^{p}\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}x_{i}&amp;x_{j}&amp;x_{k}\\
y_{i}&amp;y_{j}&amp;y_{k}\\
z_{i}&amp;z_{j}&amp;z_{k}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>p</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>p</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>p</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>p</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 2^{p}\sum_{i&lt;j&lt;k}\max(E^{p}_{ij},E^{p}_{ik},E^{p}_{jk})\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}x_{i}&amp;x_{j}&amp;x_{k}\\
y_{i}&amp;y_{j}&amp;y_{k}\\
z_{i}&amp;z_{j}&amp;z_{k}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2}\leq\sum_{i&lt;j&lt;k}(E_{ij}+E_{ik}+E_{jk})^{p}\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}x_{i}&amp;x_{j}&amp;x_{k}\\
y_{i}&amp;y_{j}&amp;y_{k}\\
z_{i}&amp;z_{j}&amp;z_{k}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex60"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\left(\Big(\sum_{i&lt;j}E^{p}_{ij}\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}x_{i}&amp;x_{j}\\
y_{i}&amp;y_{j}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2}\Big)^{1/p}+\Big(\sum_{i&lt;k}E^{p}_{ik}\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}x_{i}&amp;x_{k}\\
z_{i}&amp;z_{k}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2}\Big)^{1/p}+\Big(\sum_{j&lt;k}E^{p}_{jk}\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}y_{j}&amp;y_{k}\\
z_{j}&amp;z_{k}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2}\Big)^{1/p}\right)^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>p</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>p</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>p</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">y</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">z</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\left(\Big(\sum_{i&lt;j}E^{p}_{ij}\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}x_{i}&amp;x_{j}\\
y_{i}&amp;y_{j}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2}\Big)^{1/p}+\Big(\sum_{i&lt;k}E^{p}_{ik}\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}x_{i}&amp;x_{k}\\
z_{i}&amp;z_{k}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2}\Big)^{1/p}+\Big(\sum_{j&lt;k}E^{p}_{jk}\left|\left|\begin{smallmatrix}y_{j}&amp;y_{k}\\
z_{j}&amp;z_{k}\end{smallmatrix}\right|\right|^{2}\Big)^{1/p}\right)^{p}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex61"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left(d_{p}(\textup{{x}},\textup{{y}})+d_{p}(\textup{{x}},\textup{{z}})+d_{p}(\textup{{y}},\textup{{z}})\right)^{p}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">x</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">y</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">z</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left(d_{p}(\textup{{x}},\textup{{y}})+d_{p}(\textup{{x}},\textup{{z}})+d_{p}(\textup{{y}},\textup{{z}})\right)^{p},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p17.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p17.3.1" class="ltx_text">where the first inequality follows from Theorem <a href="#ThmThm9" title="Theorem 9. ‣ 3 A certain convexity result and the proof of the triangle inequality ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> applied to the convex map <math id="S3.p17.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(u_{1},u_{2},u_{3})\vcentcolon=\max\{u_{1},u_{2},u_{3}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(u_{1},u_{2},u_{3})\vcentcolon=\max\{u_{1},u_{2},u_{3}\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p17.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{ij}\vcentcolon=E_{ij}^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>p</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{ij}\vcentcolon=E_{ij}^{p}</annotation></semantics></math> (or in fact directly from Lemma <a href="#ThmThm10" title="Lemma 10. ‣ 3 A certain convexity result and the proof of the triangle inequality ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>), the second inequality follows from <math id="S3.p17.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(E_{ij})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(E_{ij})</annotation></semantics></math> being a distance matrix, and the third inequality follows from Corollary <a href="#ThmThm11" title="Corollary 11. ‣ 3 A certain convexity result and the proof of the triangle inequality ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a> applied to the concave map <math id="S3.p17.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(u_{1},u_{2},u_{3})\vcentcolon=\big(u_{1}^{1/p}+u_{2}^{1/p}+u_{3}^{1/p}\big)^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mn>3</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(u_{1},u_{2},u_{3})\vcentcolon=\big(u_{1}^{1/p}+u_{2}^{1/p}+u_{3}^{1/p}\big)^{p}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p17.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{ij}\vcentcolon=E_{ij}^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>p</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{ij}\vcentcolon=E_{ij}^{p}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p18" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p18.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p18.1.1" class="ltx_text">With (<a href="#S3.E44" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ 3 A certain convexity result and the proof of the triangle inequality ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">44</span></a>) proven, the proof of Theorem <a href="#ThmThm2" title="Theorem 2. ‣ 1 Introduction and main result ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> is complete and thus <math id="S3.p18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> given by (<a href="#S1.E3" title="In 1 Introduction and main result ‣ Distances between pure quantum states induced by a distance matrix" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>) is indeed a distance function on <math id="S3.p18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(\mathbb{C}^{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(\mathbb{C}^{n})</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="S3.p18.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Sx1" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section">Acknowledgements</h2>

<div id="Sx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We are grateful to Shmuel Friedland, Karol Życzkowski and Michał Eckstein for all their insightful comments and discussions. This work was supported by the National Science Centre, Poland, under the contract number 2021/03/Y/ST2/00193, within the QuantERA II Programme under Grant Agreement No 101017733, and by the European Union under ERC Advanced Grant <em id="Sx1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">TAtypic</em>, project number 101142236. RB acknowledges support by the National Science Center, Poland, under the contract number 2023/50/E/ST2/00472.</p>
</div>
